{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CghB8HWnJcCRF2qpSVpQq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_012cPkL2iDGVpozxxvxsCTHk","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium.build__20261103-202616__x53986f/work/PLAN.md","offset":361,"limit":420},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":13714,"cache_read_input_tokens":26042,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":13714},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c642ce04-34f8-46f2-be98-ceed51703e52","uuid":"7a55042c-cea1-4aa2-a2f0-d9afdaf1088f","timestamp":"2026-11-04T03:26:29.628Z","request_id":"req_011CghB8HHeSL47MQute43rp","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_012cPkL2iDGVpozxxvxsCTHk":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium.build__20261103-202616__x53986f/work/PLAN.md","offset":361,"limit":420}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012cPkL2iDGVpozxxvxsCTHk","type":"tool_result","content":"361\t---\n362\t\n363\t## 4. Systems and mechanics\n364\t\n365\tAll the numbers below are defaults in `B.T` (tuning). The **★ ones are Dev Mode sliders** (§8). Difficulty multiplies on top: Easy has monster damage ×0.7, monster HP ×0.8 and hunger ×0.5; Hard has monster damage ×1.3, monster HP ×1.25 and rest interruptions ×2.\n366\t\n367\t### 4.1 Movement and the grid\n368\t\n369\t- **The commands.**\n370\t  - Forward, back, strafe left and strafe right move one cell.\n371\t  - Turning left or right takes a quarter turn.\n372\t  - **One move is buffered** while a tween runs (the last one pressed), and a held direction repeats as soon as the tween ends.\n373\t- **Durations.** A step takes ★0.28 s and a turn ★0.20 s, eased smoothstep (the kit's `place()`). Settings → *Step animation* offers Smooth (those values), Quick (0.16 s / 0.12 s) or Instant (0 s / 0 s, as the source did).\n374\t- **When things happen.** The party's logical cell changes when the step **starts**, so targeting and monster adjacency use the new cell at once. Arrival effects happen when the step **ends**: plates, pits, teleporters, spinners, trap plates, item messages and auto-hints.\n375\t- **Blocked moves.** A wall, a closed door, gate or secret wall, a monster, or the boss blocks a move. The view lurches forward and back (the kit's `bump`), a thud plays, and a message shows at most once every 2 s:\n376\t  - \"You can't go that way.\"\n377\t  - \"The gate will not budge.\"\n378\t  - \"Something blocks the way!\" (a monster)\n379\t  - \"It is locked.\" (a locked door)\n380\t- **Head bob.** A 0.8-unit dip on each step. It is off under *reduce motion*.\n381\t- **Stairs.** Entering a stair cell fades out over 0.4 s, shows the floor card (the floor's name in the title font and one line of flavour, 1.6 s, skippable with any button), fades in at the paired arrival cell and autosaves.\n382\t  - Floor 1's up-stair is sealed: \"The grate above is bolted fast. There is no way back.\"\n383\t\n384\t### 4.2 Dungeon features and the wiring language\n385\t\n386\tEvery feature is data in `15-data-floors.js` (§7.4). Each wall feature is a `THING` drawn on the wall face (§6.2).\n387\t\n388\t| Feature | Map / table | Behaviour | Interaction (✕ / F / click) |\n389\t|---|---|---|---|\n390\t| Wooden door `+` | map | swings on hinges; monsters can't pass a closed one | ✕ facing it: open or close |\n391\t| Gate (portcullis) `=` | map + wiring | rises and falls (0.9 s); passable when open > 0.85 | none; the wiring opens it |\n392\t| Locked door `L` / `K` | map + `lock: keyId, kind: 'simple'\\|'warded'` | opens with its key; the key is used up (\"The Iron Key turns. The door opens.\") | ✕ with the key in the Hand or anywhere in a pack (it picks the right one); a thief can pick a *simple* lock |\n393\t| Magic seal `M` | map | a door of runes; opens to the Unlatch spell, scroll or wand | cast Unlatch while facing it |\n394\t| Secret wall `H` | map + wiring | looks exactly like a wall; slides into the floor (1.2 s, grinding) when wired | none; a loose stone, a catch or an event opens it |\n395\t| Illusory wall `I` | map | looks exactly like a wall; walks like floor; passing through plays a 0.15 s dissolve flash and \"The wall is an illusion!\" | walk into it |\n396\t| Pressure plate `P` | map + wiring | down while the party, any item or a medium or large monster is on it. Modes: `hold` (open while down), `latch` (stays done once triggered), `toggle` | stand on it, put an item down on it, throw an item onto it |\n397\t| Dart trap `T` | map | on entry fires darts at 2 members for ★1d4 each (\"Darts fly from the walls!\") | a thief sees it glint; a thief facing it with ✕ disarms it (DEX check: 50% + 10% × DEX bonus + 5% × level; a failure fires it) |\n398\t| Open pit `O` | map | entering it drops the party to the floor below at the pit's landing cell: 1d6 to each member, a camera drop and a fade. Feather Step floats over it. Items put into it fall to the landing. | none; wiring can bridge it |\n399\t| Trapdoor `o` | map | looks like floor (a thief or Find Seams shows thin seams); on entry it opens and falls as a pit, then stays an open pit | none |\n400\t| Teleporter `^` | map + `to: [x, y, dir], silent, on` | moves the party instantly. A *silent* one has no effect (the source's trick); a visible one swirls and whooshes. Wiring can switch it off. | walk in |\n401\t| Spinner `S` | map | sets a random facing on entry (from the `world` RNG stream) with a soft grinding sound (\"You feel a twisting underfoot.\"). Only the compass gives it away. | walk in |\n402\t| Stairs `<` `>` | map + `to: floor, at: [x, y, dir]` | change floors | walk in |\n403\t| Lever | wall feature | toggles up and down (clank); fires its wire on each change | ✕ facing it |\n404\t| Button | wall feature | momentary press (click); fires its wire | ✕ facing it |\n405\t| Loose stone / catch | wall feature | a subtle, visible odd stone or brass rivet (not invisible); glints under Find Seams or the goggles; fires its wire once | ✕ facing it |\n406\t| Alcove | wall feature + `holds: [items], accepts: filter` | a niche that shows its items | ✕: take the top item into the Hand, or place the held item |\n407\t| Keyhole | part of a door or a wall feature | takes keys of its shape | ✕ with the key |\n408\t| Inscription | wall feature + `text` | a carved plaque; the text goes to the log and to Journal → Notes | ✕ or Examine facing it |\n409\t| Candle sconce | wall feature | lit or unlit; a light; part of a sequence wire | ✕ facing it: light it |\n410\t| Great Lock | wall feature (floor 4) | turns over 2.0 s; boss mechanic (§4.7.4) | ✕ facing it |\n411\t| Brazier niche | wall feature `torch` | decor light, from the level's `t` tile (the kit's NICHE trick) | none |\n412\t| Safe room | cell list | no rest interruptions there | none |\n413\t\n414\t**The wiring language** (data, designer-facing). `wires: [{ when, mode, do, fail, once }]`.\n415\t\n416\t- **Triggers (`when`):**\n417\t  - `{ lever: id }`, `{ button: id }`, `{ catch: id }`\n418\t  - `{ plate: id }` and `{ plates: [ids], all: true }`\n419\t  - `{ buttons: [ids], within: s }` (all pressed within s seconds)\n420\t  - `{ enter: [x, y], from?: dir }`, `{ leave: [x, y] }`\n421\t  - `{ alcove: id, accepts: 'kind:key' | itemId }`\n422\t  - `{ killed: [monster ids] }` or `{ group: name }`\n423\t  - `{ flag: name }`\n424\t  - `{ sequence: [feature ids], order: true }` (wrong order: `fail`)\n425\t  - `{ timer: s }` after another wire\n426\t  - `{ loops: n, at: [x, y] }` (the teleporter hint)\n427\t- **Actions (`do` / `fail`):**\n428\t  - doors: `['open'|'close'|'toggle', doorId]`\n429\t  - pits: `['bridge', pitId]`, `['pitOpen', id]`\n430\t  - teleporters: `['teleporter', id, on]`\n431\t  - moving the party or items: `['teleport', [x, y, dir]]`, `['spin']`\n432\t  - text: `['msg', textId]`, `['hint', textId]`, `['story', nodeId]`, `['cutscene', id]`\n433\t  - things in the world: `['give', itemId, [x, y] | alcoveId]`, `['spawn', type, [x, y], n]`\n434\t  - progress: `['xp', n]`, `['flag', name, value]`, `['quest', id, state]`, `['special', id]`\n435\t  - feedback: `['sfx', name]`, `['music', cue]`, `['shake', n]`, `['light', id, on]`\n436\t  - other: `['return']` (an alcove gives its item back), `['reset', ids]`\n437\t- **Lint.** The content lint (§14) checks every id and every coordinate.\n438\t- **Hints escalate.** When `Hints` is on, each puzzle carries `hints: [[seconds or loops, textId], …]`, shown when the player lingers or loops. No puzzle can softlock:\n439\t  - a spare rock sits in every plate room;\n440\t  - the riddle returns its key;\n441\t  - the Bent Key is placed at the riddle;\n442\t  - the Wand of Unlatching is placed before the magic seal;\n443\t  - the pits' landing has a ladder back up.\n444\t\n445\t### 4.3 The party: races, classes, stats, formation\n446\t\n447\t- **Stats.** STR, DEX, CON, INT and WIS each run from 3 to 18. The modifier is −2 (3–5), −1 (6–8), 0 (9–12), +1 (13–15), +2 (16–17) or +3 (18).\n448\t  - STR: melee and thrown to-hit and damage.\n449\t  - DEX: missile to-hit, Defense and cooldown (−4% per point of modifier).\n450\t  - CON: HP per level, poison resistance.\n451\t  - INT: mage slots (+1 level-1 slot at 16+).\n452\t  - WIS: cleric slots (+1 level-1 slot at 15+, +1 level-2 slot at 17+).\n453\t\n454\t| Race | Mods | Classes | Trait |\n455\t|---|---|---|---|\n456\t| Human | — | all six | gains 5% more XP |\n457\t| Dwarf | +1 CON, −1 DEX | Fighter, Cleric, Thief | resists poison 50%; has a beard |\n458\t| Elf | +1 DEX, −1 CON | Fighter, Ranger, Mage, Thief | resists Hold 50% |\n459\t| Halfling | +1 DEX, −1 STR | Fighter, Cleric, Thief | +1 to-hit with slings, darts and thrown weapons |\n460\t\n461\t| Class | HP die | To-hit bonus | Armour | Weapons | Abilities | XP × |\n462\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n463\t| Fighter | d10 | +level | all, shields | all | +1 to-hit at every level | 1.0 |\n464\t| Paladin | d10 | +level | all, shields | all | Lay on Hands: heal 2×level once per rest; Mend ×1 from level 3 | 1.2 |\n465\t| Ranger | d8 | +level | up to chain, no shield | all | two weapons with no penalty; +1 to-hit with bows and crossbows; *Tracking* (the automap shows monsters within 4 cells) | 1.15 |\n466\t| Cleric | d8 | +¾ level | up to scale, shields | blunt only: mace, flail, warhammer, staff, sling | prayers; Turn the Dead | 0.95 |\n467\t| Mage | d4 | +½ level | robes only | dagger, staff, darts, sling | spells; reads scrolls | 1.1 |\n468\t| Thief | d6 | +¾ level | leather and studded, buckler | light weapons, short bow, crossbows, darts, sling | picks simple locks (needs Lockpicks); sees and disarms traps and trapdoors; backstab ×2 damage on sleeping, held or unaware monsters | 0.9 |\n469\t\n470\t- **Off-hand weapons** take −2 to-hit, except for Rangers. **Hit points:** level 1 gets the full die plus the CON modifier; each later level gets half the die plus 1 plus the CON modifier, at least 1.\n471\t- **Formation.** Six places in three rows of two: front 1–2, middle 3–4, back 5–6. With four members, rows 1 and 2 are filled. Members are swapped in Camp → Formation, or with ✕ on two portraits in the Party screen.\n472\t  - **Row 1** melees.\n473\t  - **Row 2** melees only with *reach* weapons (spear, glaive).\n474\t  - **Row 3** uses missiles, thrown weapons and spells only.\n475\t\n476\t### 4.4 Character creation (`create` scene)\n477\t\n478\t- **The roster.** A 2×2 roster of slots, each showing **Create** or **Premade**, plus **Quick Start**, which fills all four with the premade party (§7.9).\n479\t- **Editor steps.** Each step is one big panel with ✕ to go on and ○ to go back:\n480\t  1. **Race:** 4 tiles.\n481\t  2. **Class:** the allowed ones.\n482\t  3. **Look:** ◀ ▶ through 6 presets for each race and sex. Each preset is an `E.Humanoid` option set (hair, skin, palette, hat, beard), drawn as a large live portrait.\n483\t  4. **Stats:** 4d6 drop lowest, then race modifiers, re-rolled until the class minimums are met (Fighter STR 9, Paladin STR 12 and WIS 13, Ranger STR 13 and DEX 13, Cleric WIS 9, Mage INT 9, Thief DEX 9). □ re-rolls without limit; ✕ keeps.\n484\t  5. **Name:** a list of 12 suggestions for the race; △ picks a random one; □ opens the on-screen keyboard, a 10×4 letter grid (✕ types, □ deletes, R1 for case, Options when done). Physical keys type directly.\n485\t- **Starting gear by class.**\n486\t  - Fighter: long sword, wooden shield, leather armour.\n487\t  - Paladin: long sword, wooden shield, chain shirt.\n488\t  - Ranger: two short swords, leather armour.\n489\t  - Cleric: mace, Key of the Threshold (holy symbol), leather armour.\n490\t  - Mage: dagger and spellbook (Spark Dart, Find Seams, Slumber), plus a Traveller's Robe.\n491\t  - Thief: short sword, darts ×6, leather armour, Lockpicks.\n492\t  - Everyone gets 1 Ration and starts at food 100%.\n493\t- **Begin the Descent** starts the intro cutscene.\n494\t\n495\t### 4.5 Items, inventory, equipment and the Hand\n496\t\n497\t- **Slots for each member.** `head, neck, body, arms` (bracers), `main, off` (hands), `ring1, ring2, feet, quiver`, plus a **backpack of 12**.\n498\t  - Two-handed items fill main and lock off.\n499\t  - Ammo (bolts, arrows, sling stones) and darts stack up to 30; nothing else stacks.\n500\t  - There is no weight.\n501\t- **The Hand.** The party holds one item at a time, as the source held one on the mouse cursor. With the mouse it follows the cursor; otherwise it sits above the cards, bottom centre, with its name.\n502\t  - **Use ✕** with an item in the Hand:\n503\t    - facing an alcove, it places the item;\n504\t    - facing a keyhole with a fitting key, it inserts it;\n505\t    - with no target, it stows the item in the first free pack slot (the selected member first).\n506\t  - **Hold ✕ for 0.4 s** (**H** on the keyboard) puts it down on the front cell's floor, or on your own cell if the front is blocked. Putting it down on a plate presses the plate; putting it into a pit drops it to the landing.\n507\t  - **Throw ○** (**G**) sends it forward up to ★4 cells (+1 at STR 16+).\n508\t    - It passes over pits and plates.\n509\t    - It stops before walls and closed doors and lands in the last open cell, pressing a plate if it lands on one.\n510\t    - It stops at the first monster and hits it: thrown weapons do their dice plus STR; other items do 1d2. It then drops in that cell.\n511\t- **Picking up.** Picking up (✕ with nothing in the Hand) takes the top item in the front cell if it is open and free of monsters, otherwise in your own cell. Floor items show at the 4 quadrant spots; a fifth item and more show as a little pile.\n512\t- **Use** (□ in the Party screen):\n513\t  - eat a ration, drink a potion;\n514\t  - read a scroll (a mage casts it at once, or uses Scribe at camp to learn it);\n515\t  - read a note;\n516\t  - zap a wand (as a hand action when it is held).\n517\t- **Monster drops.** Each monster has a drop table rolled on the `loot` stream (§7.6). Named monsters have fixed drops. Thieving Latchkins drop what they stole.\n518\t- **Rust.** A Rustling's hit can rust a metal main-hand weapon (−2 damage, up to −4, shown as \"Rusted\"). It is permanent; spare weapons are placed.\n519\t\n520\t### 4.6 Combat (real time)\n521\t\n522\t- **Every hand is an action.** Using a hand does what its item does:\n523\t\n524\t  | Item in the hand | What using it does |\n525\t  |---|---|\n526\t  | weapon | attacks the front cell, if the member's row may reach it |\n527\t  | missile weapon | fires ammo from the quiver along the facing line, up to 6 cells |\n528\t  | thrown weapon (dagger, darts, hand axe, spear) | throws it |\n529\t  | spellbook or holy symbol | opens the cast menu |\n530\t  | wand | zaps |\n531\t  | shield | **Brace**: +3 Defense for 2 s |\n532\t  | nothing | punches (1d2) |\n533\t\n534\t  Using a hand starts its cooldown: the weapon's speed (§7.7) × ★attack cooldown × (1 − 0.04 × DEX modifier). Casting a spell puts **both** of the caster's hands on 2.5 s.\n535\t- **Party Strike** (□, Space, right-click in the view). Every member whose main hand is ready, and whose main-hand item can act from their row, acts at once:\n536\t  - the front row melees;\n537\t  - row 2 attacks with reach weapons;\n538\t  - anyone holding a missile or thrown weapon fires it.\n539\t\n540\t  Spellbooks and holy symbols are skipped, because a spell needs a choice. With nothing in front, the front row \"swings at the air.\"\n541\t- **To-hit.** d20 + to-hit bonus (class) + STR modifier (melee and thrown) or DEX modifier (missile) + weapon bonus + ★party to-hit + buffs ≥ the target's Defense.\n542\t  - A natural 20 always hits for double dice; a natural 1 always misses.\n543\t  - Damage is the weapon's dice + STR modifier (1.5× for two-handed weapons), × ★party damage, at least 1.\n544\t  - A miss shows MISS on the hand slot.\n545\t- **Party Defense.** 10 + armour + shield + DEX modifier + helm, bracers and rings + buffs.\n546\t- **Monster attacks.** A monster's attack roll is d20 + its attack bonus ≥ the member's Defense; its damage is its dice × ★monster damage.\n547\t- **Who gets hit.** It depends on where the attacker stands relative to the party's facing:\n548\t  - from the front: a random conscious member of the front-most occupied row;\n549\t  - from the left: the left column (places 1, 3, 5), front-most first;\n550\t  - from the right: the right column (2, 4, 6);\n551\t  - from behind: the back-most occupied row.\n552\t\n553\t  The HUD shows red chevrons on the edge the hit came from (§5.2), and the hit sound is panned.\n554\t- **Projectiles** (bolts, arrows, darts, thrown items, Spark Darts, Locking Bolts) move cell by cell at their own speed (8 cells/s for missiles, 6 for Spark Dart, 5 for monster bolts) and hit the first creature in their path.\n555\t  - A monster bolt reaching the party's cell hits the party, through the side it came from.\n556\t  - A party projectile hits the monster in the target cell's slot nearest the shooter's column.\n557\t  - Spent ammo drops in the cell where it stopped, with a 50% chance to be recovered.\n558\t- **Statuses** (seconds left, in `member.status` and `mon.status`):\n559\t\n560\t  | Status | Effect |\n561\t  |---|---|\n562\t  | Poisoned | 1 HP every 6 s for 60 s, or until Purge or an Antidote |\n563\t  | Held | can't act for 4 to 10 s; Free Hinge or the Lidless Ward prevents it |\n564\t  | Asleep (monsters) | wakes when damaged; takes ×2 damage |\n565\t  | Slowed | intervals ×1.5 |\n566\t  | Blessed / Steady | +1 to-hit and +1 to saves |\n567\t  | Warded | an absorb pool |\n568\t  | Floating | over pits; no plates |\n569\t  | Seeing | secrets glint |\n570\t  | Turned | undead flee |\n571\t\n572\t  A **save** is a d20 roll ≥ 15 − level/2 − WIS or CON modifier.\n573\t\n574\t### 4.7 Monsters and their AI\n575\t\n576\t#### 4.7.1 Size and cells\n577\t- Small monsters take 1 of 4 units in a cell, medium 2 and large 4; a cell holds 4 units.\n578\t- Monsters never enter the party's cell or walls, closed doors or pits. Fliers ignore pits and plates.\n579\t- Small monsters don't weigh plates; medium and large ones do.\n580\t\n581\t#### 4.7.2 Minds (per type in §7.6)\n582\t- **States.**\n583\t  - `asleep`: placed sleeping; noise wakes it.\n584\t  - `idle` and `patrol`: a list of cells to walk.\n585\t  - `hunt`: paths to the party with `E.Grid` A*. Cells that are full are blocked, so others take the side and back cells, and **flanking happens on its own**.\n586\t  - `engage`: next to the party it faces, winds up and strikes.\n587\t  - `ranged`: in line with a clear view and in range, it shoots.\n588\t  - `keepAway`: casters hold 3 cells off and step back if you close in.\n589\t  - `flee`: cowards below 25% HP run for 6 s; thieves flee after a steal.\n590\t  - `turned`, `held`, `asleep`.\n591\t- **Awareness.**\n592\t  - A monster becomes aware when the party's cell is in its sight radius (★sight) and its field of view (E.Fog-style shadowcasting from the monster, or the symmetric check `fog.visible` from the party, as the kit does).\n593\t  - **Noise** (combat, doors, levers, falls) wakes monsters within 4 cells; hounds hear to 6.\n594\t  - A monster forgets the party after 12 s out of sight and goes back to `patrol`.\n595\t- **Movement.** One cell per `move` seconds (per type), drawn as a glide.\n596\t\n597\t#### 4.7.3 Attacks\n598\t- **Every melee attack telegraphs.** The wind-up (★0.5 s; heavy monsters 0.8 s) is a visible animation with a sound. The strike lands only if the party is still next to the monster when the wind-up ends; otherwise \"The rat's bite snaps on air.\" **This makes the sidestep a skill.**\n599\t- **Re-engaging.** After the party changes cell, a monster next to it waits ★0.6 s before starting a new wind-up (the \"dance\" is fair but not free).\n600\t- **Intervals.** Each type has its own interval × ★monster interval.\n601\t\n602\t#### 4.7.4 The Bolt-Holder (boss, floor 4)\n603\t\n604\tIt hovers over the arena's centre cell (6,3) with **HP ★320** and Defense 15. It is immune to Hold, Sleep and Poison, and it **absorbs lightning**: Forked Lightning heals it for half, and it gloats \"The Bolt-Holder drinks the lightning!\"\n605\t\n606\t| Phase | When | Behaviour |\n607\t|---|---|---|\n608\t| **1: Caged** | the start | It takes ×0.2 damage through the cage and attacks every 3.5 s. Each of the 3 **Great Locks** (west, east and north walls) turned with ✕ (2.0 s, during which the party can't act) slides out 2 of its 7 bolts (\"The Bolt-Holder shrieks!\"). When all 3 are turned, the cage opens. |\n609\t| **2: Unbolted** | all locks turned | It takes full damage, attacks every 2.8 s and **drifts** one cell toward the party's flank every 4 s (it never enters pillar cells). At 50% HP it **relocks** one lock at random (\"It wrenches a bolt home!\"): damage taken is ×0.5 until that lock is turned again. |\n610\t| **3: Wrath** | HP below 25% | It attacks every 2.2 s and summons 2 Gazers every 12 s (4 at most). |\n611\t\n612\tIts attacks, picked by its position and line of sight:\n613\t- **Chain Lightning** (any phase): telegraphed for 0.8 s by a cyan glow and a flicker along the row or column toward the party. The bolt runs along the line until a pillar or wall: 3d6 to 2 members. Leave the line, or put a pillar between you, to dodge it.\n614\t- **Locking Gaze:** the iris narrows for 1.0 s, then 1 or 2 members without the Lidless Ward or Free Hinge are Held for 4 s (\"Your joints lock!\"). It needs line of sight, and pillars block it.\n615\t- **Bolt Rain:** marks the party's cell and 2 open neighbouring cells with glowing rings (`world.arc`) for 1.5 s, then iron bolts slam down: 2d6 to 2 members if the party is still in a marked cell.\n616\t- **Cage Slam** (adjacent only): 2d8 to the side facing it.\n617\t\n618\tOn death the Eye cracks, the bolts fly off, and the north lock wall becomes the **Stair to the Light** (✕ there starts the ending).\n619\t\n620\t### 4.8 Magic\n621\t\n622\t- **Mages** cast from their **spellbook** (an off-hand item). The book holds the spells they know; new ones come from scrolls through Camp → Scribe, which always succeeds and uses up the scroll.\n623\t- **Clerics** need their **holy symbol** in a hand. They may prepare any prayer of a level they can cast.\n624\t- **Memorizing.** Both choose what fills their slots in Camp → Memorize or Pray. The choice persists (\"same as before\" is the default), and slots refill after a full rest. Casting spends a slot.\n625\t- **Scrolls.** A mage can cast a scroll directly, and the scroll is used up. The Scroll of Raising works for clerics and paladins.\n626\t- **Wands** have charges and anyone can use one.\n627\t- **Slots by caster level, 1 to 8:**\n628\t\n629\t  | Caster | Spell level | Lv1 | Lv2 | Lv3 | Lv4 | Lv5 | Lv6 | Lv7 | Lv8 |\n630\t  |---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n631\t  | Mage | 1 | 1 | 2 | 2 | 3 | 3 | 4 | 4 | 4 |\n632\t  | Mage | 2 | 0 | 0 | 1 | 2 | 2 | 2 | 3 | 3 |\n633\t  | Mage | 3 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 1 | 2 | 2 | 3 |\n634\t  | Cleric | 1 | 1 | 2 | 2 | 3 | 3 | 3 | 4 | 4 |\n635\t  | Cleric | 2 | 0 | 0 | 1 | 2 | 2 | 3 | 3 | 3 |\n636\t  | Cleric | 3 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 1 | 1 | 2 | 2 |\n637\t\n638\t  Bonus slots come from INT and WIS (§4.3) and from the Robe of the Lintel (+1 level-1 slot).\n639\t- **Targets.**\n640\t  - `front`: the cell in front.\n641\t  - `line`: down the facing line.\n642\t  - `member`: picked on the cards.\n643\t  - `party`.\n644\t  - `door`: the door in front.\n645\t- **Spell effects** are × ★spell power. The spell list is in §7.8.\n646\t\n647\t### 4.9 Camp, rest and food\n648\t\n649\t- **Camp** (L3, C, or the HUD's camp icon) is refused while any aware monster is within 6 cells: \"You may not rest with enemies near.\"\n650\t- **Camp menu tiles:** Rest, Memorize, Pray, Scribe, Formation, Eat, Save Game, Load Game, Settings and Leave Camp.\n651\t- **Resting.** An hour passes every 0.4 s of real time. Each hour every conscious member heals ★1 + CON modifier (at least 1) × ★rest heal.\n652\t  - After 8 hours, slots refill to the prepared spells, Lay on Hands returns, and Down members wake at 1 HP.\n653\t  - During rest, clerics first cast their prepared Mends on the wounded (as the source let the party do), then pray to restore them.\n654\t  - Rest stops early when everyone is full and every slot is ready, or when ○ is pressed.\n655\t- **Interruptions.** Each hour has a ★4% chance (0 in safe rooms and once the floor's wanderer budget is spent: floor 1: 3, floor 2: 3, floor 3: 4, floor 4: 0) of spawning a wanderer group from the floor's spawn list, 2 cells away and aware. \"You are awakened by something moving!\" The camp closes.\n656\t- **Food** runs 0 to 100 for each member.\n657\t  - It drains −1 every ★60 s of play and −15 per full rest. ★Hunger rate scales it.\n658\t  - At 25: \"Cobb is hungry.\" At 0: \"Cobb is starving!\" A starving member loses 1 HP every 30 s and heals nothing from rest.\n659\t  - A Ration gives +50 and an Iron Ration +100. Loaves of the Hearth fills everyone.\n660\t  - **Eat** at camp feeds every member below 60% from the party's smallest food items.\n661\t\n662\t### 4.10 Experience, levels and hidden deeds\n663\t\n664\t- **XP for kills** is split evenly among conscious members, then × class and race multipliers and × ★XP gain.\n665\t- **Base thresholds:** level 2 at 100, 3 at 250, 4 at 500, 5 at 900, 6 at 1500, 7 at 2400 and 8 at 3600 (the demo's cap).\n666\t- **Discoveries.** A found secret gives +25 to each member and plays the `secret` sting. There are 3, marked `secret: true` in the floor data: the floor 1 closet (SW1/H1), the floor 1 illusory wall (I1) and the floor 2 catch (SW2). A hidden deed (special quest) gives +100 to each member, plays a jingle and shows \"A hidden deed is done!\". There are 3 deeds in all; Journal → Deeds counts them.\n667\t- **Level-up.** On the next rest or at once (the default is at once, with the \"level up\" sting): new HP, to-hit and slots, a portrait smile and a toast \"Brannoc has reached level 3!\".\n668\t- **Target pace** (the bot checks it, §14): about level 3 at the end of floor 1, 4 at the end of floor 2, 5 on floor 3, and 5 or 6 at the boss.\n669\t\n670\t### 4.11 Down, death, raising and game over\n671\t\n672\t- **Down.** At 0 HP a member is **Down**: unconscious, greyed portrait, can't act. A Down member hit again becomes **Dead** (bones on the card).\n673\t- **Waking.** Healing wakes a Down member at the healed amount; a full rest wakes them at 1 HP.\n674\t- **Raising the dead.** Raise from Rest (cleric spell level 3), the Scroll of Raising (2 placed) or the **Shrine of the Threshold** (floor 2 Vault, one use) brings a dead member back at 1 HP.\n675\t- **Game over.** If no member is conscious, the screen reads \"THE PARTY IS LOST\" over the frozen view, with Load last save, Load game and Title.\n676\t\n677\t### 4.12 NPCs, dialogue and choices\n678\t\n679\t- **Recruits.** Three NPCs can join, up to 6 in the party: **Tamsin Pell** (floor 1), **Durgan Copperhand** (floor 2) and **Sister Veil** (floor 3). Their scripts are in §7.9.\n680\t- **Dismissing.** Dismiss is in the Party screen, behind a confirm. A dismissed NPC goes home and is gone for good.\n681\t- **How it runs.** Dialogue is `E.Story` nodes through `E.Dialog`:\n682\t  - the speaker's live rig portrait, its mouth moving as it speaks;\n683\t  - a **babble voice** (§6.5);\n684\t  - choices picked with the d-pad and ✕, or a click;\n685\t  - story flags kept in the save (`story.state()`).\n686\t- **Veil's choice** changes floor 3 (§7.4.3).\n687\t- **Barks.** Short, non-modal lines (`modal: false, auto: 2`) for Snick, the Bolt-Holder and party barks.\n688\t\n689\t### 4.13 Messages, Examine, Journal, notes and hints\n690\t\n691\t- **The log.** The three newest lines at the bottom left, fading after 8 s; the full history is in Journal → Log.\n692\t- **Examine** (R3, X or middle click) describes what is in front in the source's voice, for example:\n693\t  - \"A wall of slick stone. One stone sits proud of the rest.\"\n694\t  - \"The Drain Rat looks badly hurt.\"\n695\t  - \"A Rusty Dagger and a Rock lie here.\"\n696\t- **The Journal** (from the Party and Map screens or the pause menu) has four tabs:\n697\t  - **Quests**: the main thread, the NPCs and Veil.\n698\t  - **Notes**: every inscription and note read, readable again.\n699\t  - **Deeds**: found out of 3.\n700\t  - **Log**.\n701\t- **Hints** (Settings → Hints, on by default) are first-time tips that use the player's own glyphs, for example \"Rats! Press □ to strike with everyone who's ready.\", plus each puzzle's escalation.\n702\t\n703\t### 4.14 Automap\n704\t\n705\t- **What it records.** `E.Fog` per floor, with a sight radius of 4 in the dungeon. A cell counts as seen when it is visible; walls are drawn next to seen floor.\n706\t- **The screen** (§5.3) shows:\n707\t  - walls, and doors in their states;\n708\t  - stairs, plates (once seen pressed or stood on), alcoves, inscriptions (a quill), teleporters (once used), the spinner (once noticed);\n709\t  - NPCs, the party arrow, and monster dots for a Ranger's Tracking.\n710\t- **A minimap** in the top-right is *optional*. The default HUD has only the compass, to keep the 10-foot view clean.\n711\t\n712\t### 4.15 Saves\n713\t\n714\t- **Where.** The engine's `game.saves`: 3 slots plus the autosave.\n715\t  - Save and Load sit in Camp and in the pause menu (when out of combat, `saves.canSave`).\n716\t  - The autosave runs on every floor arrival and after the boss.\n717\t- **The title.** Continue loads `latest()`.\n718\t- **Hub sessions.** The client gives the page in-memory storage, so add no code. Hide Save and Load in a session.\n719\t\n720\t### 4.16 Settings (the engine's, plus a *Game* group)\n721\t\n722\t- **The engine's own:** volume, music, effects, mute, reduce motion, shake and flashes, pixel scaling, screen filter, frame rate, the 3D Display settings (cards or puppets, resolution, shadows, filter) and Controls (rebinding, dead zone, vibration, **Button symbols: PlayStation / Xbox**).\n723\t- **Ours** (`game.settings.define`, group 'Game'):\n724\t\n725\t  | Setting | Options | Default |\n726\t  |---|---|---|\n727\t  | Difficulty | Easy / Normal / Hard | Normal |\n728\t  | Time in menus | Pause / Slow / Real time | Slow |\n729\t  | Step animation | Smooth / Quick / Instant | Smooth |\n730\t  | Head bob | on / off | on |\n731\t  | Hints | on / off | on |\n732\t  | Level up | At once / On rest | At once |\n733\t  | Voices volume | slider | 0.8 |\n734\t\n735\t---\n736\t\n737\t## 5. UI and UX: 10-foot, controller-first\n738\t\n739\t### 5.1 Principles\n740\t\n741\t- **Resolution.** `res: 'ps1'` with `expand: true`. The HUD is laid out for **320×240 (4:3) up to about 427×240 (16:9)** in game pixels and anchored to `r.W` and `r.H`.\n742\t  - At 1080p one game pixel is about 4.5 screen pixels, so the 5×7 font reads at about 31 px from the sofa.\n743\t  - Body text is the normal 5×7 font; headings use `scale: 2`; nothing interactive uses the tiny 3×5 font.\n744\t- **Few, big things.** At most about 12 focusable things per screen region. Every screen shows ○ Back at the bottom right. Cut density before you shrink anything.\n745\t- **One look: \"lockwork brass.\"**\n746\t  - Panels: `bg ['#1c1813', '#0e0c0a']`, border `#b8924a`, focus `#ffd36a` (double border plus a slow pulse), text `#f0e6d0`.\n747\t  - Stat colours: HP `#e0463c`, spell slots `#4a8aff`, food `#c8a040`.\n748\t  - Rivets: 2×2 dots `#e8c878` in the panel corners.\n749\t  - Title text: `E.font.title` with `colors ['#fff6d8', '#ffd36a', '#c8923a', '#6a4a1a']` and `depthColor '#2a1a08'`.\n750\t- **Keyboard and mouse are native, not stand-ins.** The same screens, with hover moving the focus, click acting, drag and drop in the Party screen, the mouse wheel scrolling lists and the Hand following the cursor (§5.4).\n751\t- **Prompts always follow `input.lastDevice`** (§5.5).\n752\t\n753\t### 5.2 The play HUD (over the full-screen 3D view)\n754\t\n755\t| Element | Where (game pixels) | Content |\n756\t|---|---|---|\n757\t| Compass | top centre, 64×16 | \"W  **N**  E\", with the facing letter at scale 2. It changes instantly on spinners: the only clue. |\n758\t| Floor toast | top left | the floor's name for 3 s on arrival |\n759\t| Party bar | bottom, `H−50` to `H−2` | one card per member in formation order. Row groups are 4 px apart, with tiny labels FRONT, MID and BACK above them. |\n760\t| Card (about 66×46) | — | live portrait 30×30 (`drawPortrait`, wince when hurt, grey when Down, bones when Dead); the name (cut to 7 letters); HP bar and `hp/max`; a 2-px food strip under the portrait; **two hand slots** 15×15 with the item icon, a cooldown wipe (dark, sweeping), a \"ready\" glint and MISS or damage pops; status icons in a row of 6×6 (poison drop, chain, Zz, shield, bowl) |\n761\t| Selected card | — | brass double frame; the L2 and R2 glyph badges under its hand slots |\n762\t| Log | above the bar, left | 3 lines, newest at the bottom, with a shadow |\n763\t| Prompts | above the bar, right | up to 4 `[glyph] Verb`, e.g. `✕ Pull lever · □ Strike · △ Party · Create Map` |\n764\t| Hand | above the bar, centre | held item icon and its name (unless the mouse cursor carries it) |\n765\t| Hit chevrons | screen edges | red chevrons on the left, right or bottom edge for 0.6 s on flank or rear hits; a red vignette on front-row hits |\n766\t| Mouse helpers | top right under the engine corner | small icons for Map, Camp, Party and Journal, mouse only; hidden for the pad |\n767\t| Boss bar | under the compass | THE BOLT-HOLDER, 200×6, with 3 lock pips (turned or locked) |\n768\t| Race HUD | top left | timer `02:13.4`, checkpoint label, crowns, and in a session the standings in seat colours |\n769\t\n770\tKeep clear of `game.cornerArea()`, the engine's top-right menu button.\n771\t\n772\t### 5.3 Screens\n773\t\n774\tEvery screen is drawn over the dimmed 3D view, takes focus navigation (§5.4) and shows its prompts.\n775\t\n776\t- **Party (△, I).**\n777\t  - **Top:** member tabs, one 32-px portrait each (L1 and R1 switch).\n778\t  - **Left:** the paperdoll, a large live rig portrait framed by 20×20 slots: Head, Neck, Body, Arms, Main, Off, Ring, Ring, Feet, Quiver.\n779\t  - **Centre:** the backpack, 4×3 slots of 22×22.\n780\t  - **Right:** details: a 32×32 icon, the name, a type line, stats (damage, speed, Defense, classes) and the description (§7.7 tone)."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c642ce04-34f8-46f2-be98-ceed51703e52","uuid":"01eee5e3-9dbb-4b82-839b-bc2521b8c85f","timestamp":"2026-11-04T03:26:29.790Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium.build__20261103-202616__x53986f/work/PLAN.md","content":"---\n\n## 4. Systems and mechanics\n\nAll the numbers below are defaults in `B.T` (tuning). The **★ ones are Dev Mode sliders** (§8). Difficulty multiplies on top: Easy has monster damage ×0.7, monster HP ×0.8 and hunger ×0.5; Hard has monster damage ×1.3, monster HP ×1.25 and rest interruptions ×2.\n\n### 4.1 Movement and the grid\n\n- **The commands.**\n  - Forward, back, strafe left and strafe right move one cell.\n  - Turning left or right takes a quarter turn.\n  - **One move is buffered** while a tween runs (the last one pressed), and a held direction repeats as soon as the tween ends.\n- **Durations.** A step takes ★0.28 s and a turn ★0.20 s, eased smoothstep (the kit's `place()`). Settings → *Step animation* offers Smooth (those values), Quick (0.16 s / 0.12 s) or Instant (0 s / 0 s, as the source did).\n- **When things happen.** The party's logical cell changes when the step **starts**, so targeting and monster adjacency use the new cell at once. Arrival effects happen when the step **ends**: plates, pits, teleporters, spinners, trap plates, item messages and auto-hints.\n- **Blocked moves.** A wall, a closed door, gate or secret wall, a monster, or the boss blocks a move. The view lurches forward and back (the kit's `bump`), a thud plays, and a message shows at most once every 2 s:\n  - \"You can't go that way.\"\n  - \"The gate will not budge.\"\n  - \"Something blocks the way!\" (a monster)\n  - \"It is locked.\" (a locked door)\n- **Head bob.** A 0.8-unit dip on each step. It is off under *reduce motion*.\n- **Stairs.** Entering a stair cell fades out over 0.4 s, shows the floor card (the floor's name in the title font and one line of flavour, 1.6 s, skippable with any button), fades in at the paired arrival cell and autosaves.\n  - Floor 1's up-stair is sealed: \"The grate above is bolted fast. There is no way back.\"\n\n### 4.2 Dungeon features and the wiring language\n\nEvery feature is data in `15-data-floors.js` (§7.4). Each wall feature is a `THING` drawn on the wall face (§6.2).\n\n| Feature | Map / table | Behaviour | Interaction (✕ / F / click) |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Wooden door `+` | map | swings on hinges; monsters can't pass a closed one | ✕ facing it: open or close |\n| Gate (portcullis) `=` | map + wiring | rises and falls (0.9 s); passable when open > 0.85 | none; the wiring opens it |\n| Locked door `L` / `K` | map + `lock: keyId, kind: 'simple'\\|'warded'` | opens with its key; the key is used up (\"The Iron Key turns. The door opens.\") | ✕ with the key in the Hand or anywhere in a pack (it picks the right one); a thief can pick a *simple* lock |\n| Magic seal `M` | map | a door of runes; opens to the Unlatch spell, scroll or wand | cast Unlatch while facing it |\n| Secret wall `H` | map + wiring | looks exactly like a wall; slides into the floor (1.2 s, grinding) when wired | none; a loose stone, a catch or an event opens it |\n| Illusory wall `I` | map | looks exactly like a wall; walks like floor; passing through plays a 0.15 s dissolve flash and \"The wall is an illusion!\" | walk into it |\n| Pressure plate `P` | map + wiring | down while the party, any item or a medium or large monster is on it. Modes: `hold` (open while down), `latch` (stays done once triggered), `toggle` | stand on it, put an item down on it, throw an item onto it |\n| Dart trap `T` | map | on entry fires darts at 2 members for ★1d4 each (\"Darts fly from the walls!\") | a thief sees it glint; a thief facing it with ✕ disarms it (DEX check: 50% + 10% × DEX bonus + 5% × level; a failure fires it) |\n| Open pit `O` | map | entering it drops the party to the floor below at the pit's landing cell: 1d6 to each member, a camera drop and a fade. Feather Step floats over it. Items put into it fall to the landing. | none; wiring can bridge it |\n| Trapdoor `o` | map | looks like floor (a thief or Find Seams shows thin seams); on entry it opens and falls as a pit, then stays an open pit | none |\n| Teleporter `^` | map + `to: [x, y, dir], silent, on` | moves the party instantly. A *silent* one has no effect (the source's trick); a visible one swirls and whooshes. Wiring can switch it off. | walk in |\n| Spinner `S` | map | sets a random facing on entry (from the `world` RNG stream) with a soft grinding sound (\"You feel a twisting underfoot.\"). Only the compass gives it away. | walk in |\n| Stairs `<` `>` | map + `to: floor, at: [x, y, dir]` | change floors | walk in |\n| Lever | wall feature | toggles up and down (clank); fires its wire on each change | ✕ facing it |\n| Button | wall feature | momentary press (click); fires its wire | ✕ facing it |\n| Loose stone / catch | wall feature | a subtle, visible odd stone or brass rivet (not invisible); glints under Find Seams or the goggles; fires its wire once | ✕ facing it |\n| Alcove | wall feature + `holds: [items], accepts: filter` | a niche that shows its items | ✕: take the top item into the Hand, or place the held item |\n| Keyhole | part of a door or a wall feature | takes keys of its shape | ✕ with the key |\n| Inscription | wall feature + `text` | a carved plaque; the text goes to the log and to Journal → Notes | ✕ or Examine facing it |\n| Candle sconce | wall feature | lit or unlit; a light; part of a sequence wire | ✕ facing it: light it |\n| Great Lock | wall feature (floor 4) | turns over 2.0 s; boss mechanic (§4.7.4) | ✕ facing it |\n| Brazier niche | wall feature `torch` | decor light, from the level's `t` tile (the kit's NICHE trick) | none |\n| Safe room | cell list | no rest interruptions there | none |\n\n**The wiring language** (data, designer-facing). `wires: [{ when, mode, do, fail, once }]`.\n\n- **Triggers (`when`):**\n  - `{ lever: id }`, `{ button: id }`, `{ catch: id }`\n  - `{ plate: id }` and `{ plates: [ids], all: true }`\n  - `{ buttons: [ids], within: s }` (all pressed within s seconds)\n  - `{ enter: [x, y], from?: dir }`, `{ leave: [x, y] }`\n  - `{ alcove: id, accepts: 'kind:key' | itemId }`\n  - `{ killed: [monster ids] }` or `{ group: name }`\n  - `{ flag: name }`\n  - `{ sequence: [feature ids], order: true }` (wrong order: `fail`)\n  - `{ timer: s }` after another wire\n  - `{ loops: n, at: [x, y] }` (the teleporter hint)\n- **Actions (`do` / `fail`):**\n  - doors: `['open'|'close'|'toggle', doorId]`\n  - pits: `['bridge', pitId]`, `['pitOpen', id]`\n  - teleporters: `['teleporter', id, on]`\n  - moving the party or items: `['teleport', [x, y, dir]]`, `['spin']`\n  - text: `['msg', textId]`, `['hint', textId]`, `['story', nodeId]`, `['cutscene', id]`\n  - things in the world: `['give', itemId, [x, y] | alcoveId]`, `['spawn', type, [x, y], n]`\n  - progress: `['xp', n]`, `['flag', name, value]`, `['quest', id, state]`, `['special', id]`\n  - feedback: `['sfx', name]`, `['music', cue]`, `['shake', n]`, `['light', id, on]`\n  - other: `['return']` (an alcove gives its item back), `['reset', ids]`\n- **Lint.** The content lint (§14) checks every id and every coordinate.\n- **Hints escalate.** When `Hints` is on, each puzzle carries `hints: [[seconds or loops, textId], …]`, shown when the player lingers or loops. No puzzle can softlock:\n  - a spare rock sits in every plate room;\n  - the riddle returns its key;\n  - the Bent Key is placed at the riddle;\n  - the Wand of Unlatching is placed before the magic seal;\n  - the pits' landing has a ladder back up.\n\n### 4.3 The party: races, classes, stats, formation\n\n- **Stats.** STR, DEX, CON, INT and WIS each run from 3 to 18. The modifier is −2 (3–5), −1 (6–8), 0 (9–12), +1 (13–15), +2 (16–17) or +3 (18).\n  - STR: melee and thrown to-hit and damage.\n  - DEX: missile to-hit, Defense and cooldown (−4% per point of modifier).\n  - CON: HP per level, poison resistance.\n  - INT: mage slots (+1 level-1 slot at 16+).\n  - WIS: cleric slots (+1 level-1 slot at 15+, +1 level-2 slot at 17+).\n\n| Race | Mods | Classes | Trait |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Human | — | all six | gains 5% more XP |\n| Dwarf | +1 CON, −1 DEX | Fighter, Cleric, Thief | resists poison 50%; has a beard |\n| Elf | +1 DEX, −1 CON | Fighter, Ranger, Mage, Thief | resists Hold 50% |\n| Halfling | +1 DEX, −1 STR | Fighter, Cleric, Thief | +1 to-hit with slings, darts and thrown weapons |\n\n| Class | HP die | To-hit bonus | Armour | Weapons | Abilities | XP × |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Fighter | d10 | +level | all, shields | all | +1 to-hit at every level | 1.0 |\n| Paladin | d10 | +level | all, shields | all | Lay on Hands: heal 2×level once per rest; Mend ×1 from level 3 | 1.2 |\n| Ranger | d8 | +level | up to chain, no shield | all | two weapons with no penalty; +1 to-hit with bows and crossbows; *Tracking* (the automap shows monsters within 4 cells) | 1.15 |\n| Cleric | d8 | +¾ level | up to scale, shields | blunt only: mace, flail, warhammer, staff, sling | prayers; Turn the Dead | 0.95 |\n| Mage | d4 | +½ level | robes only | dagger, staff, darts, sling | spells; reads scrolls | 1.1 |\n| Thief | d6 | +¾ level | leather and studded, buckler | light weapons, short bow, crossbows, darts, sling | picks simple locks (needs Lockpicks); sees and disarms traps and trapdoors; backstab ×2 damage on sleeping, held or unaware monsters | 0.9 |\n\n- **Off-hand weapons** take −2 to-hit, except for Rangers. **Hit points:** level 1 gets the full die plus the CON modifier; each later level gets half the die plus 1 plus the CON modifier, at least 1.\n- **Formation.** Six places in three rows of two: front 1–2, middle 3–4, back 5–6. With four members, rows 1 and 2 are filled. Members are swapped in Camp → Formation, or with ✕ on two portraits in the Party screen.\n  - **Row 1** melees.\n  - **Row 2** melees only with *reach* weapons (spear, glaive).\n  - **Row 3** uses missiles, thrown weapons and spells only.\n\n### 4.4 Character creation (`create` scene)\n\n- **The roster.** A 2×2 roster of slots, each showing **Create** or **Premade**, plus **Quick Start**, which fills all four with the premade party (§7.9).\n- **Editor steps.** Each step is one big panel with ✕ to go on and ○ to go back:\n  1. **Race:** 4 tiles.\n  2. **Class:** the allowed ones.\n  3. **Look:** ◀ ▶ through 6 presets for each race and sex. Each preset is an `E.Humanoid` option set (hair, skin, palette, hat, beard), drawn as a large live portrait.\n  4. **Stats:** 4d6 drop lowest, then race modifiers, re-rolled until the class minimums are met (Fighter STR 9, Paladin STR 12 and WIS 13, Ranger STR 13 and DEX 13, Cleric WIS 9, Mage INT 9, Thief DEX 9). □ re-rolls without limit; ✕ keeps.\n  5. **Name:** a list of 12 suggestions for the race; △ picks a random one; □ opens the on-screen keyboard, a 10×4 letter grid (✕ types, □ deletes, R1 for case, Options when done). Physical keys type directly.\n- **Starting gear by class.**\n  - Fighter: long sword, wooden shield, leather armour.\n  - Paladin: long sword, wooden shield, chain shirt.\n  - Ranger: two short swords, leather armour.\n  - Cleric: mace, Key of the Threshold (holy symbol), leather armour.\n  - Mage: dagger and spellbook (Spark Dart, Find Seams, Slumber), plus a Traveller's Robe.\n  - Thief: short sword, darts ×6, leather armour, Lockpicks.\n  - Everyone gets 1 Ration and starts at food 100%.\n- **Begin the Descent** starts the intro cutscene.\n\n### 4.5 Items, inventory, equipment and the Hand\n\n- **Slots for each member.** `head, neck, body, arms` (bracers), `main, off` (hands), `ring1, ring2, feet, quiver`, plus a **backpack of 12**.\n  - Two-handed items fill main and lock off.\n  - Ammo (bolts, arrows, sling stones) and darts stack up to 30; nothing else stacks.\n  - There is no weight.\n- **The Hand.** The party holds one item at a time, as the source held one on the mouse cursor. With the mouse it follows the cursor; otherwise it sits above the cards, bottom centre, with its name.\n  - **Use ✕** with an item in the Hand:\n    - facing an alcove, it places the item;\n    - facing a keyhole with a fitting key, it inserts it;\n    - with no target, it stows the item in the first free pack slot (the selected member first).\n  - **Hold ✕ for 0.4 s** (**H** on the keyboard) puts it down on the front cell's floor, or on your own cell if the front is blocked. Putting it down on a plate presses the plate; putting it into a pit drops it to the landing.\n  - **Throw ○** (**G**) sends it forward up to ★4 cells (+1 at STR 16+).\n    - It passes over pits and plates.\n    - It stops before walls and closed doors and lands in the last open cell, pressing a plate if it lands on one.\n    - It stops at the first monster and hits it: thrown weapons do their dice plus STR; other items do 1d2. It then drops in that cell.\n- **Picking up.** Picking up (✕ with nothing in the Hand) takes the top item in the front cell if it is open and free of monsters, otherwise in your own cell. Floor items show at the 4 quadrant spots; a fifth item and more show as a little pile.\n- **Use** (□ in the Party screen):\n  - eat a ration, drink a potion;\n  - read a scroll (a mage casts it at once, or uses Scribe at camp to learn it);\n  - read a note;\n  - zap a wand (as a hand action when it is held).\n- **Monster drops.** Each monster has a drop table rolled on the `loot` stream (§7.6). Named monsters have fixed drops. Thieving Latchkins drop what they stole.\n- **Rust.** A Rustling's hit can rust a metal main-hand weapon (−2 damage, up to −4, shown as \"Rusted\"). It is permanent; spare weapons are placed.\n\n### 4.6 Combat (real time)\n\n- **Every hand is an action.** Using a hand does what its item does:\n\n  | Item in the hand | What using it does |\n  |---|---|\n  | weapon | attacks the front cell, if the member's row may reach it |\n  | missile weapon | fires ammo from the quiver along the facing line, up to 6 cells |\n  | thrown weapon (dagger, darts, hand axe, spear) | throws it |\n  | spellbook or holy symbol | opens the cast menu |\n  | wand | zaps |\n  | shield | **Brace**: +3 Defense for 2 s |\n  | nothing | punches (1d2) |\n\n  Using a hand starts its cooldown: the weapon's speed (§7.7) × ★attack cooldown × (1 − 0.04 × DEX modifier). Casting a spell puts **both** of the caster's hands on 2.5 s.\n- **Party Strike** (□, Space, right-click in the view). Every member whose main hand is ready, and whose main-hand item can act from their row, acts at once:\n  - the front row melees;\n  - row 2 attacks with reach weapons;\n  - anyone holding a missile or thrown weapon fires it.\n\n  Spellbooks and holy symbols are skipped, because a spell needs a choice. With nothing in front, the front row \"swings at the air.\"\n- **To-hit.** d20 + to-hit bonus (class) + STR modifier (melee and thrown) or DEX modifier (missile) + weapon bonus + ★party to-hit + buffs ≥ the target's Defense.\n  - A natural 20 always hits for double dice; a natural 1 always misses.\n  - Damage is the weapon's dice + STR modifier (1.5× for two-handed weapons), × ★party damage, at least 1.\n  - A miss shows MISS on the hand slot.\n- **Party Defense.** 10 + armour + shield + DEX modifier + helm, bracers and rings + buffs.\n- **Monster attacks.** A monster's attack roll is d20 + its attack bonus ≥ the member's Defense; its damage is its dice × ★monster damage.\n- **Who gets hit.** It depends on where the attacker stands relative to the party's facing:\n  - from the front: a random conscious member of the front-most occupied row;\n  - from the left: the left column (places 1, 3, 5), front-most first;\n  - from the right: the right column (2, 4, 6);\n  - from behind: the back-most occupied row.\n\n  The HUD shows red chevrons on the edge the hit came from (§5.2), and the hit sound is panned.\n- **Projectiles** (bolts, arrows, darts, thrown items, Spark Darts, Locking Bolts) move cell by cell at their own speed (8 cells/s for missiles, 6 for Spark Dart, 5 for monster bolts) and hit the first creature in their path.\n  - A monster bolt reaching the party's cell hits the party, through the side it came from.\n  - A party projectile hits the monster in the target cell's slot nearest the shooter's column.\n  - Spent ammo drops in the cell where it stopped, with a 50% chance to be recovered.\n- **Statuses** (seconds left, in `member.status` and `mon.status`):\n\n  | Status | Effect |\n  |---|---|\n  | Poisoned | 1 HP every 6 s for 60 s, or until Purge or an Antidote |\n  | Held | can't act for 4 to 10 s; Free Hinge or the Lidless Ward prevents it |\n  | Asleep (monsters) | wakes when damaged; takes ×2 damage |\n  | Slowed | intervals ×1.5 |\n  | Blessed / Steady | +1 to-hit and +1 to saves |\n  | Warded | an absorb pool |\n  | Floating | over pits; no plates |\n  | Seeing | secrets glint |\n  | Turned | undead flee |\n\n  A **save** is a d20 roll ≥ 15 − level/2 − WIS or CON modifier.\n\n### 4.7 Monsters and their AI\n\n#### 4.7.1 Size and cells\n- Small monsters take 1 of 4 units in a cell, medium 2 and large 4; a cell holds 4 units.\n- Monsters never enter the party's cell or walls, closed doors or pits. Fliers ignore pits and plates.\n- Small monsters don't weigh plates; medium and large ones do.\n\n#### 4.7.2 Minds (per type in §7.6)\n- **States.**\n  - `asleep`: placed sleeping; noise wakes it.\n  - `idle` and `patrol`: a list of cells to walk.\n  - `hunt`: paths to the party with `E.Grid` A*. Cells that are full are blocked, so others take the side and back cells, and **flanking happens on its own**.\n  - `engage`: next to the party it faces, winds up and strikes.\n  - `ranged`: in line with a clear view and in range, it shoots.\n  - `keepAway`: casters hold 3 cells off and step back if you close in.\n  - `flee`: cowards below 25% HP run for 6 s; thieves flee after a steal.\n  - `turned`, `held`, `asleep`.\n- **Awareness.**\n  - A monster becomes aware when the party's cell is in its sight radius (★sight) and its field of view (E.Fog-style shadowcasting from the monster, or the symmetric check `fog.visible` from the party, as the kit does).\n  - **Noise** (combat, doors, levers, falls) wakes monsters within 4 cells; hounds hear to 6.\n  - A monster forgets the party after 12 s out of sight and goes back to `patrol`.\n- **Movement.** One cell per `move` seconds (per type), drawn as a glide.\n\n#### 4.7.3 Attacks\n- **Every melee attack telegraphs.** The wind-up (★0.5 s; heavy monsters 0.8 s) is a visible animation with a sound. The strike lands only if the party is still next to the monster when the wind-up ends; otherwise \"The rat's bite snaps on air.\" **This makes the sidestep a skill.**\n- **Re-engaging.** After the party changes cell, a monster next to it waits ★0.6 s before starting a new wind-up (the \"dance\" is fair but not free).\n- **Intervals.** Each type has its own interval × ★monster interval.\n\n#### 4.7.4 The Bolt-Holder (boss, floor 4)\n\nIt hovers over the arena's centre cell (6,3) with **HP ★320** and Defense 15. It is immune to Hold, Sleep and Poison, and it **absorbs lightning**: Forked Lightning heals it for half, and it gloats \"The Bolt-Holder drinks the lightning!\"\n\n| Phase | When | Behaviour |\n|---|---|---|\n| **1: Caged** | the start | It takes ×0.2 damage through the cage and attacks every 3.5 s. Each of the 3 **Great Locks** (west, east and north walls) turned with ✕ (2.0 s, during which the party can't act) slides out 2 of its 7 bolts (\"The Bolt-Holder shrieks!\"). When all 3 are turned, the cage opens. |\n| **2: Unbolted** | all locks turned | It takes full damage, attacks every 2.8 s and **drifts** one cell toward the party's flank every 4 s (it never enters pillar cells). At 50% HP it **relocks** one lock at random (\"It wrenches a bolt home!\"): damage taken is ×0.5 until that lock is turned again. |\n| **3: Wrath** | HP below 25% | It attacks every 2.2 s and summons 2 Gazers every 12 s (4 at most). |\n\nIts attacks, picked by its position and line of sight:\n- **Chain Lightning** (any phase): telegraphed for 0.8 s by a cyan glow and a flicker along the row or column toward the party. The bolt runs along the line until a pillar or wall: 3d6 to 2 members. Leave the line, or put a pillar between you, to dodge it.\n- **Locking Gaze:** the iris narrows for 1.0 s, then 1 or 2 members without the Lidless Ward or Free Hinge are Held for 4 s (\"Your joints lock!\"). It needs line of sight, and pillars block it.\n- **Bolt Rain:** marks the party's cell and 2 open neighbouring cells with glowing rings (`world.arc`) for 1.5 s, then iron bolts slam down: 2d6 to 2 members if the party is still in a marked cell.\n- **Cage Slam** (adjacent only): 2d8 to the side facing it.\n\nOn death the Eye cracks, the bolts fly off, and the north lock wall becomes the **Stair to the Light** (✕ there starts the ending).\n\n### 4.8 Magic\n\n- **Mages** cast from their **spellbook** (an off-hand item). The book holds the spells they know; new ones come from scrolls through Camp → Scribe, which always succeeds and uses up the scroll.\n- **Clerics** need their **holy symbol** in a hand. They may prepare any prayer of a level they can cast.\n- **Memorizing.** Both choose what fills their slots in Camp → Memorize or Pray. The choice persists (\"same as before\" is the default), and slots refill after a full rest. Casting spends a slot.\n- **Scrolls.** A mage can cast a scroll directly, and the scroll is used up. The Scroll of Raising works for clerics and paladins.\n- **Wands** have charges and anyone can use one.\n- **Slots by caster level, 1 to 8:**\n\n  | Caster | Spell level | Lv1 | Lv2 | Lv3 | Lv4 | Lv5 | Lv6 | Lv7 | Lv8 |\n  |---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n  | Mage | 1 | 1 | 2 | 2 | 3 | 3 | 4 | 4 | 4 |\n  | Mage | 2 | 0 | 0 | 1 | 2 | 2 | 2 | 3 | 3 |\n  | Mage | 3 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 1 | 2 | 2 | 3 |\n  | Cleric | 1 | 1 | 2 | 2 | 3 | 3 | 3 | 4 | 4 |\n  | Cleric | 2 | 0 | 0 | 1 | 2 | 2 | 3 | 3 | 3 |\n  | Cleric | 3 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 1 | 1 | 2 | 2 |\n\n  Bonus slots come from INT and WIS (§4.3) and from the Robe of the Lintel (+1 level-1 slot).\n- **Targets.**\n  - `front`: the cell in front.\n  - `line`: down the facing line.\n  - `member`: picked on the cards.\n  - `party`.\n  - `door`: the door in front.\n- **Spell effects** are × ★spell power. The spell list is in §7.8.\n\n### 4.9 Camp, rest and food\n\n- **Camp** (L3, C, or the HUD's camp icon) is refused while any aware monster is within 6 cells: \"You may not rest with enemies near.\"\n- **Camp menu tiles:** Rest, Memorize, Pray, Scribe, Formation, Eat, Save Game, Load Game, Settings and Leave Camp.\n- **Resting.** An hour passes every 0.4 s of real time. Each hour every conscious member heals ★1 + CON modifier (at least 1) × ★rest heal.\n  - After 8 hours, slots refill to the prepared spells, Lay on Hands returns, and Down members wake at 1 HP.\n  - During rest, clerics first cast their prepared Mends on the wounded (as the source let the party do), then pray to restore them.\n  - Rest stops early when everyone is full and every slot is ready, or when ○ is pressed.\n- **Interruptions.** Each hour has a ★4% chance (0 in safe rooms and once the floor's wanderer budget is spent: floor 1: 3, floor 2: 3, floor 3: 4, floor 4: 0) of spawning a wanderer group from the floor's spawn list, 2 cells away and aware. \"You are awakened by something moving!\" The camp closes.\n- **Food** runs 0 to 100 for each member.\n  - It drains −1 every ★60 s of play and −15 per full rest. ★Hunger rate scales it.\n  - At 25: \"Cobb is hungry.\" At 0: \"Cobb is starving!\" A starving member loses 1 HP every 30 s and heals nothing from rest.\n  - A Ration gives +50 and an Iron Ration +100. Loaves of the Hearth fills everyone.\n  - **Eat** at camp feeds every member below 60% from the party's smallest food items.\n\n### 4.10 Experience, levels and hidden deeds\n\n- **XP for kills** is split evenly among conscious members, then × class and race multipliers and × ★XP gain.\n- **Base thresholds:** level 2 at 100, 3 at 250, 4 at 500, 5 at 900, 6 at 1500, 7 at 2400 and 8 at 3600 (the demo's cap).\n- **Discoveries.** A found secret gives +25 to each member and plays the `secret` sting. There are 3, marked `secret: true` in the floor data: the floor 1 closet (SW1/H1), the floor 1 illusory wall (I1) and the floor 2 catch (SW2). A hidden deed (special quest) gives +100 to each member, plays a jingle and shows \"A hidden deed is done!\". There are 3 deeds in all; Journal → Deeds counts them.\n- **Level-up.** On the next rest or at once (the default is at once, with the \"level up\" sting): new HP, to-hit and slots, a portrait smile and a toast \"Brannoc has reached level 3!\".\n- **Target pace** (the bot checks it, §14): about level 3 at the end of floor 1, 4 at the end of floor 2, 5 on floor 3, and 5 or 6 at the boss.\n\n### 4.11 Down, death, raising and game over\n\n- **Down.** At 0 HP a member is **Down**: unconscious, greyed portrait, can't act. A Down member hit again becomes **Dead** (bones on the card).\n- **Waking.** Healing wakes a Down member at the healed amount; a full rest wakes them at 1 HP.\n- **Raising the dead.** Raise from Rest (cleric spell level 3), the Scroll of Raising (2 placed) or the **Shrine of the Threshold** (floor 2 Vault, one use) brings a dead member back at 1 HP.\n- **Game over.** If no member is conscious, the screen reads \"THE PARTY IS LOST\" over the frozen view, with Load last save, Load game and Title.\n\n### 4.12 NPCs, dialogue and choices\n\n- **Recruits.** Three NPCs can join, up to 6 in the party: **Tamsin Pell** (floor 1), **Durgan Copperhand** (floor 2) and **Sister Veil** (floor 3). Their scripts are in §7.9.\n- **Dismissing.** Dismiss is in the Party screen, behind a confirm. A dismissed NPC goes home and is gone for good.\n- **How it runs.** Dialogue is `E.Story` nodes through `E.Dialog`:\n  - the speaker's live rig portrait, its mouth moving as it speaks;\n  - a **babble voice** (§6.5);\n  - choices picked with the d-pad and ✕, or a click;\n  - story flags kept in the save (`story.state()`).\n- **Veil's choice** changes floor 3 (§7.4.3).\n- **Barks.** Short, non-modal lines (`modal: false, auto: 2`) for Snick, the Bolt-Holder and party barks.\n\n### 4.13 Messages, Examine, Journal, notes and hints\n\n- **The log.** The three newest lines at the bottom left, fading after 8 s; the full history is in Journal → Log.\n- **Examine** (R3, X or middle click) describes what is in front in the source's voice, for example:\n  - \"A wall of slick stone. One stone sits proud of the rest.\"\n  - \"The Drain Rat looks badly hurt.\"\n  - \"A Rusty Dagger and a Rock lie here.\"\n- **The Journal** (from the Party and Map screens or the pause menu) has four tabs:\n  - **Quests**: the main thread, the NPCs and Veil.\n  - **Notes**: every inscription and note read, readable again.\n  - **Deeds**: found out of 3.\n  - **Log**.\n- **Hints** (Settings → Hints, on by default) are first-time tips that use the player's own glyphs, for example \"Rats! Press □ to strike with everyone who's ready.\", plus each puzzle's escalation.\n\n### 4.14 Automap\n\n- **What it records.** `E.Fog` per floor, with a sight radius of 4 in the dungeon. A cell counts as seen when it is visible; walls are drawn next to seen floor.\n- **The screen** (§5.3) shows:\n  - walls, and doors in their states;\n  - stairs, plates (once seen pressed or stood on), alcoves, inscriptions (a quill), teleporters (once used), the spinner (once noticed);\n  - NPCs, the party arrow, and monster dots for a Ranger's Tracking.\n- **A minimap** in the top-right is *optional*. The default HUD has only the compass, to keep the 10-foot view clean.\n\n### 4.15 Saves\n\n- **Where.** The engine's `game.saves`: 3 slots plus the autosave.\n  - Save and Load sit in Camp and in the pause menu (when out of combat, `saves.canSave`).\n  - The autosave runs on every floor arrival and after the boss.\n- **The title.** Continue loads `latest()`.\n- **Hub sessions.** The client gives the page in-memory storage, so add no code. Hide Save and Load in a session.\n\n### 4.16 Settings (the engine's, plus a *Game* group)\n\n- **The engine's own:** volume, music, effects, mute, reduce motion, shake and flashes, pixel scaling, screen filter, frame rate, the 3D Display settings (cards or puppets, resolution, shadows, filter) and Controls (rebinding, dead zone, vibration, **Button symbols: PlayStation / Xbox**).\n- **Ours** (`game.settings.define`, group 'Game'):\n\n  | Setting | Options | Default |\n  |---|---|---|\n  | Difficulty | Easy / Normal / Hard | Normal |\n  | Time in menus | Pause / Slow / Real time | Slow |\n  | Step animation | Smooth / Quick / Instant | Smooth |\n  | Head bob | on / off | on |\n  | Hints | on / off | on |\n  | Level up | At once / On rest | At once |\n  | Voices volume | slider | 0.8 |\n\n---\n\n## 5. UI and UX: 10-foot, controller-first\n\n### 5.1 Principles\n\n- **Resolution.** `res: 'ps1'` with `expand: true`. The HUD is laid out for **320×240 (4:3) up to about 427×240 (16:9)** in game pixels and anchored to `r.W` and `r.H`.\n  - At 1080p one game pixel is about 4.5 screen pixels, so the 5×7 font reads at about 31 px from the sofa.\n  - Body text is the normal 5×7 font; headings use `scale: 2`; nothing interactive uses the tiny 3×5 font.\n- **Few, big things.** At most about 12 focusable things per screen region. Every screen shows ○ Back at the bottom right. Cut density before you shrink anything.\n- **One look: \"lockwork brass.\"**\n  - Panels: `bg ['#1c1813', '#0e0c0a']`, border `#b8924a`, focus `#ffd36a` (double border plus a slow pulse), text `#f0e6d0`.\n  - Stat colours: HP `#e0463c`, spell slots `#4a8aff`, food `#c8a040`.\n  - Rivets: 2×2 dots `#e8c878` in the panel corners.\n  - Title text: `E.font.title` with `colors ['#fff6d8', '#ffd36a', '#c8923a', '#6a4a1a']` and `depthColor '#2a1a08'`.\n- **Keyboard and mouse are native, not stand-ins.** The same screens, with hover moving the focus, click acting, drag and drop in the Party screen, the mouse wheel scrolling lists and the Hand following the cursor (§5.4).\n- **Prompts always follow `input.lastDevice`** (§5.5).\n\n### 5.2 The play HUD (over the full-screen 3D view)\n\n| Element | Where (game pixels) | Content |\n|---|---|---|\n| Compass | top centre, 64×16 | \"W  **N**  E\", with the facing letter at scale 2. It changes instantly on spinners: the only clue. |\n| Floor toast | top left | the floor's name for 3 s on arrival |\n| Party bar | bottom, `H−50` to `H−2` | one card per member in formation order. Row groups are 4 px apart, with tiny labels FRONT, MID and BACK above them. |\n| Card (about 66×46) | — | live portrait 30×30 (`drawPortrait`, wince when hurt, grey when Down, bones when Dead); the name (cut to 7 letters); HP bar and `hp/max`; a 2-px food strip under the portrait; **two hand slots** 15×15 with the item icon, a cooldown wipe (dark, sweeping), a \"ready\" glint and MISS or damage pops; status icons in a row of 6×6 (poison drop, chain, Zz, shield, bowl) |\n| Selected card | — | brass double frame; the L2 and R2 glyph badges under its hand slots |\n| Log | above the bar, left | 3 lines, newest at the bottom, with a shadow |\n| Prompts | above the bar, right | up to 4 `[glyph] Verb`, e.g. `✕ Pull lever · □ Strike · △ Party · Create Map` |\n| Hand | above the bar, centre | held item icon and its name (unless the mouse cursor carries it) |\n| Hit chevrons | screen edges | red chevrons on the left, right or bottom edge for 0.6 s on flank or rear hits; a red vignette on front-row hits |\n| Mouse helpers | top right under the engine corner | small icons for Map, Camp, Party and Journal, mouse only; hidden for the pad |\n| Boss bar | under the compass | THE BOLT-HOLDER, 200×6, with 3 lock pips (turned or locked) |\n| Race HUD | top left | timer `02:13.4`, checkpoint label, crowns, and in a session the standings in seat colours |\n\nKeep clear of `game.cornerArea()`, the engine's top-right menu button.\n\n### 5.3 Screens\n\nEvery screen is drawn over the dimmed 3D view, takes focus navigation (§5.4) and shows its prompts.\n\n- **Party (△, I).**\n  - **Top:** member tabs, one 32-px portrait each (L1 and R1 switch).\n  - **Left:** the paperdoll, a large live rig portrait framed by 20×20 slots: Head, Neck, Body, Arms, Main, Off, Ring, Ring, Feet, Quiver.\n  - **Centre:** the backpack, 4×3 slots of 22×22.\n  - **Right:** details: a 32×32 icon, the name, a type line, stats (damage, speed, Defense, classes) and the description (§7.7 tone).","numLines":420,"startLine":361,"totalLines":2145}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_012cPkL2iDGVpozxxvxsCTHk","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
