{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CghB8aDs5xHbM3caYnMbR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01CJG8VyaUDv9TT7vZJ3BBxW","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium.build__20261103-202616__x53986f/work/PLAN.md","offset":781,"limit":420},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":15197,"cache_read_input_tokens":39756,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":15197},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c642ce04-34f8-46f2-be98-ceed51703e52","uuid":"e8165f2d-9a2d-4cd4-8ccf-6b7fdd1df486","timestamp":"2026-11-04T03:26:33.135Z","request_id":"req_011CghB8Zxk96uiiKbsow1tR","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01CJG8VyaUDv9TT7vZJ3BBxW":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium.build__20261103-202616__x53986f/work/PLAN.md","offset":781,"limit":420}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CJG8VyaUDv9TT7vZJ3BBxW","type":"tool_result","content":"781\t  - **Bottom:** `HP 11/11 · Defense 14 · Lv 2 Fighter · XP 140/250 · Food ███░`.\n782\t  - **Actions:** ✕ takes or places (it carries the item into the Hand, or swaps), □ Use, △ Drop at your feet, R2 Sheet. ○ returns a carried item, then closes the screen.\n783\t  - **The Sheet tab** shows the stats and their modifiers, class abilities, resistances and the spellbook or the prayers. Dismiss (NPCs) is here, behind a confirm.\n784\t- **Cast.** Opened by a caster's book or symbol hand.\n785\t  - A centred panel of about 260×150, with level tabs L1, L2, L3 (shoulders switch them).\n786\t  - Rows read \"Spark Dart ×2\", with a description and the target type.\n787\t  - ✕ casts. A `member` target then moves the highlight across the cards (◀ ▶, ✕). A `line`, `front`, `door` or `party` spell fires at once. ○ cancels.\n788\t- **Camp (L3, C).** The view darkens and a small campfire light glows in the cell. Tiles in 2 rows of 5 (§4.9).\n789\t  - **Rest** shows a rest panel: the hours counting, HP ticking up on the cards and ○ Stop.\n790\t  - **Memorize** and **Pray**: known spells on the left (grouped by level, with descriptions) and slots on the right. ✕ on a spell fills the next free slot of its level, ✕ on a slot empties it, △ \"Same as before\".\n791\t  - **Scribe**: scrolls in the party's packs that the mage doesn't know; ✕ learns one.\n792\t  - **Formation**: the 2×3 places; ✕ twice swaps two members.\n793\t  - **Eat**: a confirm, then a summary of who ate what.\n794\t  - **Save** and **Load** open the engine's slot screens (`saves.show`).\n795\t  - **Settings** opens `game.menu('settings')`.\n796\t- **Map (Create, M).**\n797\t  - A parchment-coloured panel with the floor's explored cells at 8 to 10 px per cell, and a legend row at the bottom.\n798\t  - L1 and R1 switch between visited floors; the d-pad or stick pans a map larger than the screen; ○ closes.\n799\t  - Dev *reveal* shows everything.\n800\t- **Journal (J, or the tab from Party or Map).** Quests, Notes, Deeds and Log. Notes open the **Reader**, a parchment page with the note's text at the normal size, paged with the d-pad.\n801\t- **Dialogue.** `E.Dialog` at the bottom: portrait on the left, name in brass and 3 lines a page. ✕ finishes the line, then turns the page; ○ fast-forwards; choices are a vertical list.\n802\t- **Title.**\n803\t  - **The view.** The Drain-gate stage from the intro (§7.3, stage B) at night. The camera pushes slowly toward the grate, the torches flicker, and every 12 s the great bolt slides home with a shake and a thud.\n804\t  - **The logo.** **EYE OF THE BOLT-HOLDER** in `E.font.title`, scale 4, brass colours (§5.1), with a slow glint across it, and \"A thousand locks. One eye.\" under it.\n805\t  - **The menu,** a centred `E.Menu`: Continue (only when a save exists), New Game, Load Game, Rat Run, Settings, About & Credits.\n806\t  - **The bottom line:** the prompts for the last device and the version (`E.versionLabel()`, plus the game's own version).\n807\t  - **Music:** `title`.\n808\t  - **The attract mode** starts after 10 s idle (§9). The touch notice is shown on touch-only devices (§5.7).\n809\t- **Creation:** §4.4. **The floor card:** §4.1. **About and Credits:** §11. **Touch notice:** §5.7.\n810\t- **Game over.** \"THE PARTY IS LOST\" in the title font over the frozen, darkened view; one line from the floor (\"The Drains keep what they take.\"); then Load last save · Load game · Title.\n811\t- **Ending.** The ending cutscene (§7.3), then the credits roll (the §11 Credits page, scrolling), then the stats panel (time, kills, secrets 3, deeds 3, deaths, levels) and Title. The `ending` song plays.\n812\t\n813\t### 5.4 Focus navigation and the mouse\n814\t\n815\t- **One focus system** (`61-ui-kit.js`) for every screen.\n816\t  - Each screen registers its widgets as rects with an id, an action and optional explicit neighbours.\n817\t  - The d-pad and the left stick (menus use the engine's `up/down/left/right`, which include the stick) move to the nearest widget in that direction, by geometry; explicit neighbours override.\n818\t  - Holding a direction repeats (`input.repeat`, 0.35 s, then 0.1 s).\n819\t- **The mouse.**\n820\t  - Moving the pointer over a widget focuses it; a left click acts as ✕; a right click on a slot acts as □; the wheel scrolls lists.\n821\t  - Party screen drag and drop: mouse-down carries the item, mouse-up places it.\n822\t- **Mouse in the 3D view.** Each frame, project the interactables in front with `world.project`: the front wall's feature, the items in the front and own cells, doors, the monsters in front and alcoves. Each gets a screen hotspot.\n823\t  - Hovering one outlines it (a soft brass rim drawn with the pen around the thing) and shows a tooltip, e.g. \"Lever — click to pull\".\n824\t  - A left click on a hotspot uses it. With an item in the Hand, a left click on the lower view puts it down and a left click on the upper view throws it, as in the source.\n825\t  - A right click anywhere in the view is **Party Strike**.\n826\t- **Party cards.** A click on a hand slot uses that hand (the source's core gesture); a click on a portrait selects; a right click on a portrait opens that member in the Party screen.\n827\t\n828\t### 5.5 Prompts and glyphs\n829\t\n830\t- **One painter, `glyph(g, x, y, action)`**, draws a badge for the action's binding on the last device:\n831\t\n832\t  | Device | Badge |\n833\t  |---|---|\n834\t  | Pad, PlayStation (default) | ✕ blue, ○ red, □ pink, △ green, drawn as shapes on a dark disc; L1, R1, L2, R2, L3, R3, Options and Create as rounded labels; D-pad and stick icons |\n835\t  | Pad, Xbox (Settings → Controls → Button symbols) | A green, B red, X blue, Y yellow letters; LB, RB, LT, RT, View, Menu |\n836\t  | Keyboard | a keycap with the bound key (`input.codeLabel`) |\n837\t  | Mouse | a mouse icon with the left or right button lit |\n838\t\n839\t  Never print raw codes. Build every prompt string from `input.label(action)` through the painter, so rebinding just works.\n840\t- **When the prompts change.** They switch the moment `lastDevice` changes: a pad button or a stick past the dead zone, a key, or a mouse move of more than 4 px or a click.\n841\t\n842\t### 5.6 Input map (all rebindable except the menu actions)\n843\t\n844\t| Action | Gamepad (standard mapping) | Keyboard | Mouse |\n845\t|---|---|---|---|\n846\t| Step forward / back | Left stick ↑ ↓, D-pad ↑ ↓ | W / S, ↑ / ↓, Numpad 8 / 5 or 2 | — |\n847\t| Strafe left / right | Left stick ← → | A / D, Numpad 4 / 6 | — |\n848\t| Turn left / right | D-pad ← →, right stick ← → (a flick, repeating every 0.35 s while held) | Q / E, ← / →, Numpad 7 / 9 | — |\n849\t| Use / interact / take / place / stow | ✕ (tap) | F | left click on a thing in the view |\n850\t| Put the Hand's item down | ✕ (hold 0.4 s) | H | left click on the lower view |\n851\t| Throw the Hand's item | ○ | G | left click on the upper view |\n852\t| Party Strike | □ | Space | right click in the view |\n853\t| Select member previous / next | L1 / R1 | Tab / Shift+Tab, or 1–6 | click a portrait |\n854\t| Selected member's main / off hand | R2 / L2 | 1–6 main hand (and select); Shift+1–6 off hand | click a hand slot |\n855\t| Party screen | △ | I | portrait right click, HUD icon |\n856\t| Camp | L3 | C | HUD icon |\n857\t| Examine ahead | R3 | X | middle click |\n858\t| Automap | Create (acts on release; ignored when Options was pressed while Create was held) | M | HUD icon |\n859\t| Journal | (from the Party or Map tabs, or the pause menu) | J | HUD icon |\n860\t| Pause menu | Options | Esc, P | the engine's corner button |\n861\t| Menus | D-pad / stick, ✕ confirm, ○ back, L1 / R1 tabs | arrows, Enter, Backspace or Esc | hover, click, wheel |\n862\t\n863\t**Implementation notes.**\n864\t- Define your own play actions (`fwd, back, strafeL, strafeR, turnL, turnR, use, strike, selPrev, selNext, handMain, handOff, party, camp, examine, map, journal, throw, putDown`) in the play scene's `input` map, as the kit did.\n865\t- **Don't use the engine's merged `left/right` in play**: they merge the d-pad and the stick, and here they mean different things.\n866\t  - Read the left stick from `input.padAxes[0]` and `[1]`, with the dead zone and a 0.5 threshold, for move and strafe.\n867\t  - Read the right stick X from `padAxes[2]`, as a flick with re-arm, for turning.\n868\t  - The d-pad codes are `Pad12` to `Pad15`.\n869\t- **Hub rule.** While Create (`Pad8`) is held, ignore Options (`Pad9`), and don't toggle the map on Create's release if Options went down in between.\n870\t- **Idle detection** (attract mode): any action pressed, any `input.held` code, a stick past 0.3, a pointer move over 4 px or a click.\n871\t\n872\t### 5.7 Touch-only devices\n873\t\n874\t- **Detection.** `matchMedia('(pointer: coarse)')` with no `(hover: hover)`, and no keyboard or gamepad input seen yet. On such devices `input.touchEnabled = false`: no touch buttons and no stick.\n875\t- **The title** shows a panel: \"**Controller or keyboard required.** Connect a controller or a keyboard to play.\" The engine's top-right menu button stays and opens Settings.\n876\t- **The attract mode runs** after the same 10 s idle. A touch exits it to the title, which shows the notice again.\n877\t- **The notice hides** the moment a key or a pad button arrives, and play works normally from then on.\n878\t\n879\t---\n880\t\n881\t## 6. Presentation: art, animation and audio\n882\t\n883\t### 6.1 Art direction\n884\t\n885\t- **The base is the engine's native 3D look,** the one the spike showed: code-drawn textures, `world.res = 'pixels'` (chunky low-res pixels), toon light, outlines on, characters as **cards** (`world.look = 'card'`: the rigs drawn as pixel art from the camera's own angle) and fog for the source's distance falloff.\n886\t- **Lighting.** `torchShadows: 2`, `torchLights: 6`, the party's lantern as a `world.light` at the eyes, and `glowLights: 4` for spells.\n887\t- **New art** wherever the source's feel needs it: wall features, doors, floor items, the creatures in §6.3, the boss, the brass UI, item icons and the stages for the title and the cutscenes.\n888\t- **Props.** For generic set dressing (bones, barrels, crates, chains, cobwebs, banners, candles, tables), search the store first with `node tools/asset-find.mjs \"bones\"`, using `kaykit-dungeon-remastered`, `kenney-mini-dungeon` and `kenney-graveyard`. Cut a set with `tools/asset-set.mjs`, load it with `E.addAssets`, and place props with `world.shape(id, …)` or `{ shape }` in the legend.\n889\t\n890\t| Floor | Ground (`level.ground`, `colors`) | Walls (`side`, `color`) | Fog | Ambient `[sky, ground, power]` | Signature dressing |\n891\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n892\t| 1 The Hasp Drains | flagstone `#3e4a44 / #2a332f / #55615a`; a floor colour function paints dark-green **water channels** (6 units wide) down the Rat Channel and Cistern cells | brick `#4a5048` | `#06080a`, 24 → 150 | `#4a5a5a, #1a201e, 2.6` | floor drains (grates), dripping pipes (pen tubes), slime streaks, rusty chains, rat bones, sluice wheels |\n893\t| 2 The Tumbler Halls | tiles `#5a4a3a / #3e3228 / #7a6450` | block `#6a5a48` | `#0a0806`, 40 → 220 | `#7a6048, #2a2018, 3.0` | turning **wall gears** (pen rings of teeth, slowly rotating), anvils, workbenches, cogs on the floor, forge glow (orange lights) in the Workshop |\n894\t| 3 The Gloam Deeps | plain `#2a2434 / #1a1622 / #3a3248` | block `#2e2838` | `#040306`, 20 → 130 | `#3a3a5a, #141220, 2.2` | carved **eye reliefs** on walls (pen), shut-eye banners, bone piles, pale blue candles in the Chapel (lights) |\n895\t| 4 The Eye's Vault | tiles `#3a3e46`; the arena floor colour function adds faint cyan rune lines | block `#30343c` | `#020204`, 30 → 200 | `#2a3040, #0c0e14, 2.0` | the boss's amber light, cyan lightning flashes, the 3 Great Locks' rune lights going out as they turn |\n896\t\n897\t- **Item icons.** Make about 60 of them as `E.sprite` strings, designed at 12×12 and drawn at ×1 on the cards and ×2 in the Party screen. Shade them with `E.tones`.\n898\t- **Item models.** Each floor item also gets a tiny **3D model drawn with the pen**, lying flat at its quadrant spot:\n899\t  - blade (sword, dagger): a thin box with a cross-guard;\n900\t  - axe or mace: a head on a haft;\n901\t  - crossbow; bolts or arrows: thin tubes;\n902\t  - potion: a ball and a neck, in its colour;\n903\t  - scroll: a tube; book: a box;\n904\t  - key: a ring plus a shaft with teeth, in the key's colour;\n905\t  - rock: a grey lump of balls; ration: a wrapped box;\n906\t  - gear: a ring of boxes; ward: a toothed disc.\n907\t\n908\t### 6.2 The 3D presenter (`40–44`)\n909\t\n910\t- **Building a floor.**\n911\t  - Map each cell to 2×2 level tiles (`#` → `##`, open → `..`). A torch wall feature turns the tile on its open side into `t`, the kit's NICHE trick.\n912\t  - Make `new E.World3D(game, { level, look: 'card', res: 'pixels', torchLights: 6, torchShadows: 2, torchPower: 18, ambient, fog, sky: fogColour, camera: { mode: 'fixed' }, overlay: { fov: 60 }, onDraw })`.\n913\t  - Create all of the floor's lights at build time (lantern, candles, forge glows, the boss), as the engine requires.\n914\t  - Build every floor's world at boot and `prepare()` it, so a floor change never compiles a shader mid-game. On a floor change, swap the active world.\n915\t- **Each frame,** from the sim state:\n916\t  - **Camera:** `world.camera.fixed = { x, y, z: EYE + bob, yaw, pitch: −0.04, fov: 74 }`, from the party's tween (the kit's `place()`). A bump adds the lurch, a hit adds `game.shake`, a pit fall drops z by 40 and fades.\n917\t  - **Doors and gates:** `world.thing('door', …, { w: 32, h: 46, swing })`; set `t.open` toward the sim's state and call `world.setSolid` when it opens.\n918\t  - **Secret walls** (and **illusory walls**): a movable wall block that is **indistinguishable from the level's walls**. Try `world.box({ fixed: true, side: <the floor's side style>, color })` first; if it doesn't match, add a `wallBlock` helper to the 3D engine that reuses the level's wall material (risk 3, §13). A secret block sinks into the floor when opened; an illusory one never moves (the party's step through it is masked by the dissolve).\n919\t  - **Wall features:** custom `E.World3D.THINGS`, drawn with the pen on the wall face (local +y out of the wall, as the kit's `wallLever`).\n920\t\n921\t    | THING | How to draw it |\n922\t    |---|---|\n923\t    | `wallLever` | the kit's |\n924\t    | `wallButton` | a square stone and a brass boss that presses in |\n925\t    | `catch` | a slightly proud stone with a crack, or a brass rivet plate; glints under Seeing |\n926\t    | `alcove` | a dark recessed box that draws its items inside |\n927\t    | `keyhole` | per key shape: iron round, warded cross, gear toothed, bone skull, ward discs |\n928\t    | `plaque` | a stone tablet with dark glyph dashes |\n929\t    | `grate`, `pipe`, `chain`, `gearWall` (rotating), `eyeRelief` | decor |\n930\t    | `candle` | a holder, a wax stick and a flame glow when lit, paired with its light |\n931\t    | `greatLock` | a big wheel with rune glow, spun over 2 s |\n932\t    | `undergate` | a great door with 3 keyholes and 7 bolt bars that slide when a ward goes in |\n933\t    | `cage` | bars |\n934\t    | `shrine` | a ring of tiny rat statues |\n935\t    | `clockFace` | a dial with 4 gear sockets and hands that move once the clock is whole |\n936\t    | `altarSlab` | a floor slab |\n937\t    | `stairs` | the kit's `stair` (down), plus `stairUp` |\n938\t    | `pitEdge` | a dark hole with a lip; a bridge slab when bridged |\n939\t    | `plate` | the kit's |\n940\t    | `teleporterField` | a soft swirl glow, only when not silent |\n941\t\n942\t  - **Floor items:** pen models at the quadrant spots of the visible cells (`onDraw`).\n943\t  - **Monsters:** cards (`world.mob` with `rig`, `blob` or `orb`) are steered toward their slot's position with `vx`/`vy` as the kit does (`fly: true` for fliers). Their `anim` comes from the sim: attack phase, hurt flash, `die` pose, sink. Pen-drawn creatures are drawn in `onDraw` from their sim state and a local animation clock (§6.3).\n944\t  - **Projectiles and FX:** `world.glow` for bolts and orbs, pen bars for lightning, `game.particles` for sparks, embers, smoke and damage `text`, and `world.arc` for floor telegraphs (Bolt Rain).\n945\t  - **First-person overlay:** with `world.overlay.pen`, draw the striking member's weapon swinging across its side of the view: left for places 1, 3 and 5, right for 2, 4 and 6. The crossbow rises and kicks; a caster's hand glows in the spell's colour.\n946\t  - **Hover outlines and name tags:** project with `world.project`, then draw them in the HUD.\n947\t- **NullView** implements the same interface (`enter(floor)`, `frame(r)`, `event(e)`, `pick(sx, sy)`) as no-ops for Node.\n948\t\n949\t### 6.3 Creature recipes\n950\t\n951\tThe sizes follow the engine's guidance (heroes `size` 1.2 to 1.4, bosses larger). Every rig gets a real palette.\n952\t\n953\t| Creature | Build | Recipe | Animation notes |\n954\t|---|---|---|---|\n955\t| Drain Rat | card, `E.Blob` | `{ R: 3.6, ears: 'cat', tail: true, feet: true, mouth: 'fangs', colors: { base: '#6a5a50', dk: '#3e342e', lt: '#9a8a7a', eye: '#ff6a4a' } }` | fast squash scurry; the wind-up is a rear-back squash |\n956\t| Bloat Leech | pen | 5 balls (r 4 → 2.5) along a sine curve on the floor, `#b89a9a` with `#7a5a5a` rings; a mouth ring of 6 small balls; a wet glint | the body undulates; it lunges out 6 units on the strike |\n957\t| Latchkin | card, `E.Humanoid` | `{ size: .85, build: 'chibi', hunch: .5, hood: true, outfit: 'tunic', bladeLen: 5, eyeGlow: '#ffd24a', colors: { skin: '#7a8a5a', hair: '#4a3a2a', cloth: '#6a4a32', pants: '#3a2e22', metal: '#9a9aa8' } }`, plus a pen ring of keys at the belt | the `thrust` move; it stays in a crouch-run while fleeing |\n958\t| Drain Ooze | card, `E.Blob` | `{ R: 8, face: 'front', mouth: true, colors: { base: '#5a8a3a', dk: '#2e5a22', lt: '#9ad06a', spec: '#e8ffd0' } }` | a slow wobble; it slams by squashing down; it splashes green particles |\n959\t| Rat Knot | pen | 6 rat-body balls in a ring with ear cones, tails as tubes knotted at the middle | the ring wobbles and turns; two bites a strike |\n960\t| Snick, the Latch-Boss | card, `E.Humanoid` | `{ size: 1.0, build: 'bulky', hunch: .3, hat: { style: 'crown', color: '#c8a040' }, armor: true, outfit: 'coat', bladeLen: 9, eyeGlow: '#ffd24a', colors: { skin: '#7a8a5a', cloth: '#5a3a2a', plate: '#a08040' } }`, plus a pen cape of hanging keys | the `overhead` move; it rattles its keys at 50% when it calls for help |\n961\t| Tinker Skeleton | card, `E.Humanoid` | `{ size: 1.2, build: 'skeleton', outfit: 'coat', bladeLen: 7, colors: { bone: '#d8cfb4', cloth: '#5a4030', metal: '#8a8a90' } }`, plus a pen hammer head on the blade | the `overhead` and `slash` moves; it collapses into bones on death |\n962\t| Rustling | card, `E.Blob` | `{ R: 4.2, horns: true, feet: true, mouth: true, colors: { base: '#b8642a', dk: '#7a3a18', lt: '#e8a060' } }` | the horns twitch; it throws rust-flake particles when it hits |\n963\t| Brass Spider | pen | abdomen ball r 7 and cephalothorax r 4.5 in `#b8923a`; 8 legs of 2 tubes each with procedural tetrapod gait (sine phase lifts); 4 red eye glows | legs step; it lunges on the strike; it falls apart into parts on death |\n964\t| Clockwork Sentinel | card, `E.Humanoid` | `{ size: 1.6, build: 'bulky', armor: true, hat: { style: 'helmet', color: '#8a6a3a' }, bladeLen: 14, eyeGlow: '#ff8a3a', colors: { cloth: '#6a4a2a', plate: '#b08a4a', metal: '#c8a868', skin: '#5a4a3a' } }`, plus a pen wind-up key turning on its back | the `twohand` move with a 0.8 s wind-up; the key spins faster during it |\n965\t| Lidless Hound | pen | a quadruped (adapt the 3D horror kit's dogs, `src/starter3d/40-horror.js`): pale `#c8b8b0`, smooth eyeless head, long jaw | run, leap and bite |\n966\t| Gloam Seer | card, `E.Humanoid` | `{ size: 1.25, build: 'heroic', outfit: 'robe', hood: true, weapon: 'staff', eyeGlow: '#8ae0ff', colors: { cloth: '#d8d0e8', hair: '#3a2a4a', skin: '#b8b0c8', trim: '#6a4a9a' } }`, plus an eye-sigil glow over the staff | the `cast` pose while charging a Locking Bolt (cyan glow growing) |\n967\t| Gloam Warden | card, `E.Humanoid` | `{ size: 1.35, build: 'heroic', armor: true, hat: { style: 'helmet', color: '#2a2434' }, weapon: 'staff', eyeGlow: '#e8e8ff', colors: { cloth: '#2a2434', plate: '#4a4458', metal: '#9a98a8', skin: '#b8b0c8' } }`, plus a pen halberd blade on the staff | the `thrust` move (reaches two cells) |\n968\t| Gazer | card orb plus pen | an orb `{ color: '#e8a040', r: 4 }`; pen iris (a flattened ball `#3a8a6a`), pupil, two lid slabs, 3 fin cones | blinks; the pupil tracks the party; it glows before Spark Gaze |\n969\t| Lockjaw Golem | card, `E.Humanoid` | `{ size: 1.9, build: 'bulky', armor: true, weapon: null, eyeGlow: '#7ad8ff', colors: { cloth: '#3a3e46', plate: '#5a606a', skin: '#4a4e56' } }`, plus a pen **padlock head** (box body and shackle tube) instead of a hat | the `haymaker` move; heavy footstep shakes |\n970\t| **The Bolt-Holder** | pen | an eye ball r 14 (sclera `#e8e0c8` with red vein bars); a flattened amber iris r 7 (`#e8a030`) facing the party; a black pupil r 3.5 that dilates; upper and lower lid slabs that blink and narrow for the Gaze; **7 radial iron bolts** (bars 22 long and 2.5 thick, with 5×5×3 heads) that slide out 2 per Great Lock (the 7th, the keystone, never moves); cyan lightning arcs (jagged pen bars) between neighbouring bolt heads; a ±3 bob; an amber `world.light`; red tint and crack lines in phase 3 | it must not read as a beholder: no eyestalks, no mouth, no tentacles. It reads as a caged iron lantern-eye. |\n971\t| Ghosts (race) | card, `E.Humanoid` | a hooded cloak in the player's seat colour, `fade 0.45`, a lantern glow in the seat colour, and the hub name as a HUD tag | they glide between the cells they report |\n972\t\n973\t**People** (portraits and cutscenes):\n974\t- the party (§7.9);\n975\t- Keywarden Imelda Strake: heroic, band crown, coat, navy and silver;\n976\t- Magister Abel Lintel: robe, pointed hat, long white hair;\n977\t- Ysolde Vane: robe, long hair, ghost blue, drawn translucent;\n978\t- Tamsin: size 0.9, ponytail, green hood;\n979\t- Durgan: bulky, braided beard, iron helmet;\n980\t- Veil: robe, hood, eyes shut (draw them closed).\n981\t\n982\t### 6.4 Animation list (new, on the engine's rigs, tweens and pen)\n983\t\n984\t- **Party view.** Step glide with bob; turn ease; bump lurch; pit fall (drop and fade); teleport (a cut or a swirl); spinner (a short wobble only when *visible*: none for silent spinners); hit shake; level-up glow on the card; KO slump (the portrait tinted grey); death toll (the card turns to bones); first-person weapon swings for each weapon family (blade, axe, blunt, spear thrust, crossbow, bow, sling, throw, punch); casting hand glows.\n985\t- **World.** Gates rising with a chain rattle and wooden doors swinging; levers flipping and buttons and catches pressing in; plates sinking; secret walls sinking; the trapdoor dropping open; the pit bridge rising; teleporter swirl; gears turning; candles lighting and guttering; the Great Locks spinning; the Undergate's 7 bolts drawing back one by one; the clock's hands moving once it is whole; the boss's bolts sliding, lids blinking, iris dilating and lightning arcing.\n986\t- **Monsters.** Idle, move glide, wind-up telegraph (the move's `wind` phase, at least 0.5 s), strike, hurt flash and recoil, death (the `die` pose, then sink; blobs squash flat; constructs fall apart into pen parts; the leech curls).\n987\t- **UI.** Cooldown wipes; damage pops; card shake; chevrons; focus pulse; toast slides; the title logo shimmer.\n988\t\n989\t### 6.5 Audio: code only, no files\n990\t\n991\t- **The music director.** It plays a song per floor through `game.audio.music(song, { fade: 1 })`. Every dungeon song carries a `fight` track (drums and bass, `on: false`) that comes in with `audio.layer('fight', 1, .5)` when any monster engages and goes out 4 s after the last one. Stings use `audio.sting`. All songs are original, in the step-sequencer format (`{ bpm, steps, tracks: [{ wave, vol, notes }] }`).\n992\t\n993\t  | Song | Feel | Seed motif (original) |\n994\t  |---|---|---|\n995\t  | `title`, \"The City of a Thousand Locks\" | 76 bpm, D minor, bell pulses over a low triangle | `D4 - F4 A4 G4 - F4 E4 \\| D4 - - - C4 E4 G4 F4 \\| E4 - D4 C#4 D4 - - -` |\n996\t  | `drains` | 60 bpm, a sparse drone, a lonely pulse every 8 bars, drips as sfx | low `A1` drone; a `pulse25` figure `A3 . C4 . E4 . . . \\| D4 . C4 . B3 . . .` |\n997\t  | `tumbler` | 96 bpm in 6/8, ticking percussion | `drums` `h . h c . h` over `E2 . B2 E2 . B2` |\n998\t  | `gloam` | 54 bpm, sine pads, a tritone colour | `C3` plus `F#3` pads, a choir-like sine line in long notes |\n999\t  | `vault` / `boss` | 138 bpm, saw bass, lightning arpeggios | `A2 A2 . A2 C3 . A2 . \\| G2 G2 . G2 Bb2 . G2 .`, arps `A4 E5 A5 E5` |\n1000\t  | `camp` | 70 bpm, a lullaby | the title motif in a major key, triangle |\n1001\t  | `ending` | 84 bpm, D major | the title motif resolved |\n1002\t  | stings | — | `levelUp`, `deed`, `secret`, `wardFound`, `gameOver`, `victory`, `npcJoin` |\n1003\t\n1004\t- **Sound effects** (`audio.define`, the engine's voice format; the kit's `SOUNDS` are the template). Define every one of these:\n1005\t  - steps per floor: wet stone, metal grating, dust, stone;\n1006\t  - turn, bump, door open and close, gate grind, lever clank, button click, catch click, plate thunk, secret-wall grind, illusion shimmer, trapdoor, fall and land;\n1007\t  - teleporter whoosh (visible ones only), spinner grind, dart volley;\n1008\t  - key turn, lock fail, lockpick scratch and snap, alcove place and take;\n1009\t  - item pickup, drop and throw whoosh, land clatter, eat crunch, drink glug, scroll unroll, wand zap;\n1010\t  - swings (blade, axe, blunt), crossbow and bow twangs, sling whirr;\n1011\t  - hits (flesh, metal, bone, ooze), miss whiff, crit clang, party hurt;\n1012\t  - level up, death toll, raise;\n1013\t  - each spell: cast, travel loop and impact;\n1014\t  - monster voices for each type (squeak, slurp, chitter, rattle, clank, growl, chant, gaze hum);\n1015\t  - boss: roar, lightning crack, bolt slam, lock turn and shriek;\n1016\t  - UI: move, confirm, back, error, tab;\n1017\t  - ambience loops per floor: drips, distant gears, whispers, a low hum.\n1018\t\n1019\t  Pan by bearing with the patched `{ pan }` (§3.9).\n1020\t- **Voices: the babble synth** (`50-audio.js`, on `game.audio.ctx` and routed to the voice bus).\n1021\t  - **Per-speaker profile:** `{ base: Hz, range: semitones, rate: syllables/s, wave, formant: ×, breath: 0..1, vib: [Hz, depth], echo: 0..1 }`. The profiles:\n1022\t\n1023\t    | Speaker | base Hz | range | rate | wave | other |\n1024\t    |---|---|---|---|---|---|\n1025\t    | Narrator | 95 | 3 | 9 | triangle | echo 0.2 |\n1026\t    | Keywarden | 170 | 4 | 12 | square | |\n1027\t    | Lintel | 120 | 5 | 10 | saw | |\n1028\t    | Tamsin | 300 | 7 | 15 | pulse | |\n1029\t    | Durgan | 105 | 4 | 11 | square | |\n1030\t    | Ysolde | 220 | 5 | 9 | sine | echo 0.4 |\n1031\t    | Veil | 240 | 3 | 10 | triangle | breath 0.5 |\n1032\t    | Snick | 260 | 8 | 16 | square | |\n1033\t    | Bolt-Holder | 70 | 6 | 8 | saw | ring mod 30 Hz, echo 0.5 |\n1034\t\n1035\t    The party members also get profiles from their race and sex.\n1036\t  - **Driving it.** Set `talk.voice = null`. Each update, read `talk.shown`; for every two new letters (and on every vowel), emit a syllable.\n1037\t  - **The syllable:**\n1038\t    - The vowel picks a formant pair (F1/F2): a 800/1200, e 400/2000, i 300/2300, o 450/800, u 325/700, × `formant`.\n1039\t    - The letter's code picks the pitch inside `range`, so a word always sounds the same.\n1040\t    - Plosives (b d g k p t) add a 10 ms noise click; fricatives (f s v z h) add a 40 ms high-passed noise; nasals (m n) add a low hum.\n1041\t    - `?` rises at the end, `!` is louder and higher, `.` pauses 0.15 s and `,` pauses 0.08 s.\n1042\t  - **The voice:** an oscillator into two parallel band-pass filters (Q 8) into a gain envelope (5 ms attack, 0.6× hold, 30 ms release), then the bus.\n1043\t  - **Barks:** short babble for party pain (\"Oof!\"), effort (\"Hah!\"), level-up (\"Yes!\") and casting, and for monster taunts.\n1044\t  - **Test it in Node.** `babble.plan(text, profile)` returns syllable events (time, pitch, F1, F2, noise) and must be deterministic (§14). In Node there is no AudioContext, so the synth is a no-op.\n1045\t\n1046\t---\n1047\t\n1048\t## 7. Content\n1049\t\n1050\t### 7.1 World bible (all original)\n1051\t\n1052\t- **Hasp, the City of a Thousand Locks.** A walled river port that grew rich on locks. Its sigil is a key crossed with a bolt. It is ruled by the **Council of Keys** under **High Keywarden Imelda Strake**, stern and practical. The city's wizard is **Magister Abel Lintel**, dry, old and worried.\n1053\t- **The Tumblerwrights' Guild.** The finest locksmiths in the world. Their halls sat under the city until a disaster sealed them a century ago. Their last guildmistress, **Ysolde Vane**, haunts the halls.\n1054\t- **The Undergate.** The guild's masterwork: a gate beneath the city's foundations that seals something older, which this demo only hints at. To watch it, the guild forged **the Watcher**, an eye that never closes, and gave it **seven Great Bolts** to hold. The Watcher learned to love holding. It now calls itself **the Bolt-Holder** and turns the locks of Hasp from below: \"Every lock is a promise. I keep them all.\"\n1055\t- **Its servants.**\n1056\t  - **Latchkins**: small sewer goblins who worship keys and steal iron. Their chief is **Snick, the Latch-Boss**.\n1057\t  - The guild's own clockwork and its dead workers, wound up again.\n1058\t  - The **Gloam-folk** of the deep, pale people who believe the Eye is a god and call themselves the **Lidless**: their Seers, Wardens and hounds.\n1059\t- **The quest.** Gather the **Three Wards** (copper from the Drains, brass from the Guild Vault, iron from the Lidless Reliquary), open the Undergate and close the Eye.\n1060\t- **The humour.** The title is playful; the prose is earnest. Wit comes in small doses: Tamsin's quips, dry item descriptions, the Rat King's crown.\n1061\t\n1062\t### 7.2 Writing style guide\n1063\t\n1064\tThe model is the source's voice: terse, second-person, past the fourth wall never.\n1065\t\n1066\t- **Messages** are one short sentence, present tense, addressed to \"you\" or naming a member. Use plain words and full stops; keep exclamation marks for danger and wonder.\n1067\t  - \"You hear a click in the distance.\"\n1068\t  - \"There is a loose stone here.\"\n1069\t  - \"The bolt will not move.\"\n1070\t  - \"This key does not fit.\"\n1071\t  - \"The Iron Key turns. The door opens.\"\n1072\t  - \"A hidden door grinds open!\"\n1073\t  - \"The wall is an illusion!\"\n1074\t  - \"The floor gives way!\"\n1075\t  - \"You feel a twisting underfoot.\"\n1076\t  - \"Nothing happens.\"\n1077\t  - \"Darts fly from the walls!\"\n1078\t  - \"Cobb is hungry.\"\n1079\t  - \"Odelia is poisoned!\"\n1080\t  - \"Brannoc swings at the air.\"\n1081\t  - \"The Drain Rat dies.\"\n1082\t  - \"You may not rest with enemies near.\"\n1083\t  - \"You are awakened by something moving!\"\n1084\t  - \"A hidden deed is done!\"\n1085\t  - \"Ysa has reached level 3!\"\n1086\t- **Inscriptions** are in CAPITALS, formal and a little archaic: \"NOT EVERY STONE IS STONE.\"\n1087\t- **Narration** (intro and ending) is stately, in the third person, with short paragraphs and one image each.\n1088\t- **NPCs** speak formally but each in their own voice:\n1089\t  - Tamsin: quick and cheeky.\n1090\t  - Durgan: gruff and practical.\n1091\t  - Ysolde: sorrowful and old-fashioned.\n1092\t  - Veil: hushed and strange, always talking about eyes.\n1093\t  - The Bolt-Holder: grand, slow, with CAPITALS for its emphasis.\n1094\t- **Item descriptions** are 1 to 2 dry sentences: \"It has seen better days, and better locks.\"\n1095\t- **Never** use modern slang, game-mechanic jargon in the fiction (say \"slots\" only in menus), or the source's names.\n1096\t\n1097\t### 7.3 Story beats and cutscenes\n1098\t\n1099\tThe cutscenes are 3D stages, small `E.World3D` sets built at boot, with rigs, a camera moved by `game.script` and `game.tween`, dialogue boxes, babble voices and stings. Any button speeds the text; holding Options or Esc for 1 s skips the cutscene.\n1100\t\n1101\t**INTRO** (about 75 s):\n1102\t- *Stage A*, the Council Hall at night: pillars, banners, two braziers, a long table, Strake and Lintel.\n1103\t- *Stage B*, the Drain-gate: a stair down into the dark, a grate, and the party's four rigs.\n1104\t\n1105\t1. NARRATOR: \"Hasp. The city of a thousand locks.\"\n1106\t2. NARRATOR: \"For three hundred years its Tumblerwrights forged the finest locks in the world, and its people slept soundly behind them.\"\n1107\t3. NARRATOR: \"Then the locks began to turn by themselves.\"\n1108\t4. STRAKE: \"Doors bolt themselves in empty houses. Wells cap shut. Last night the east granary locked forty men inside and would not open for axes.\"\n1109\t5. LINTEL: \"It comes from below. Past the Drains, past the old guild halls… from the Undergate itself.\"\n1110\t6. STRAKE: \"You were recommended to me as people who open things. Go down. Find what holds our bolts, and break its grip.\"\n1111\t7. *(Stage B)* NARRATOR: \"The Drain-gate groans open. You step down into the dark.\"\n1112\t8. NARRATOR: \"Behind you, the grate crashes shut. A great bolt slides home with a sound like a closing tomb.\"\n1113\t   - The camera shakes, a pen-drawn bolt slides across the grate, and the torches gutter.\n1114\t9. NARRATOR: \"Somewhere far below, something blinks.\"\n1115\t   - Cut to black. An amber eye opens for 0.5 s, with the boss's hum.\n1116\t10. Play begins on floor 1 with the log line \"The grate above is bolted fast. There is no way back.\"\n1117\t\n1118\t**Mid-game beats** (in-dungeon, through E.Story):\n1119\t- Tamsin freed (floor 1).\n1120\t- Snick's barks.\n1121\t- Ysolde's ghost twice (floor 2).\n1122\t- Durgan (floor 2).\n1123\t- Veil's choice (floor 3).\n1124\t- The Undergate opening (floor 3, a 10 s in-engine moment: the camera holds, seven bolts draw back one by one, a deep chord).\n1125\t- The Bolt-Holder's taunts (floor 4).\n1126\t\n1127\t**ENDING** (about 60 s):\n1128\t- *Stage C*, the Vault after the battle: light pours from the cracked Eye.\n1129\t- *Stage D*, the city square at dawn: houses, doors swinging open, Strake, Lintel and the party.\n1130\t\n1131\t1. NARRATOR: \"The Eye cracks from lid to lid, and its light goes out.\"\n1132\t2. NARRATOR: \"One by one, the seven Great Bolts fall silent.\"\n1133\t3. *(Stage D)* NARRATOR: \"Above, in the city of a thousand locks, every door swings open at once.\"\n1134\t4. STRAKE: \"Hasp is in your debt. The guild's last forge will cast your names into the Undergate itself.\"\n1135\t5. LINTEL: \"Yet the Undergate was built to keep something in. With its Watcher gone…\"\n1136\t6. NARRATOR: \"Far beneath the city, in a darkness older than locks, something tries the door.\"\n1137\t7. Title card **THE END**, then the credits roll (§11), then the stats: time, kills, secrets found out of 3, hidden deeds out of 3, deaths and the party's levels. Back to the title.\n1138\t\n1139\t### 7.4 The floors\n1140\t\n1141\t- **Legend** (one character per cell):\n1142\t\n1143\t  | Char | Meaning |\n1144\t  |---|---|\n1145\t  | `#` | wall |\n1146\t  | `.` | floor |\n1147\t  | `@` | start or arrival |\n1148\t  | `<` `>` | stairs |\n1149\t  | `+` | wooden door |\n1150\t  | `=` | gate |\n1151\t  | `L` `K` | locked door |\n1152\t  | `M` | magic seal |\n1153\t  | `H` | secret wall |\n1154\t  | `I` | illusory wall |\n1155\t  | `P` | plate |\n1156\t  | `T` | dart trap |\n1157\t  | `O` | pit |\n1158\t  | `o` | trapdoor |\n1159\t  | `^` | teleporter |\n1160\t  | `S` | spinner |\n1161\t  | `U` | the Undergate |\n1162\t  | `*` | pit landing |\n1163\t  | `B` | the boss |\n1164\t\n1165\t- **Coordinates** are (x, y) with y = 0 at the top; the rulers above each map give x.\n1166\t- **Wall features** are given as *(stand x, y, face)*.\n1167\t- **Checked during planning:** every walkthrough below was checked with a reachability script (each target reachable with only the doors opened so far, and every gated area unreachable before its gate). It came to 157 checks, including both of Veil's branches and the Sump. Your content lint repeats them (§14).\n1168\t\n1169\t#### 7.4.1 Floor 1: The Hasp Drains (22×17)\n1170\t\n1171\t*\"Cold water talks to itself in the channels. The walls sweat.\"* (floor card)\n1172\t\n1173\t```\n1174\t    0000000000111111111122\n1175\t    0123456789012345678901\n1176\t  0 ######################\n1177\t  1 #.....=.#####........#\n1178\t  2 #.....#######........#\n1179\t  3 ##+#####.########L####\n1180\t  4 ##.#####H########.####\n1181\t  5 #....###.....####.####\n1182\t  6 #....###......P.=.####\n1183\t  7 #............#########\n1184\t  8 #....###.....#########\n1185\t  9 ##.######I##.#########\n1186\t 10 ##=#####...#...T....##\n1187\t 11 ##.#####...########=##\n1188\t 12 ##.##..#...###.......#\n1189\t 13 ##..+..#######.......#\n1190\t 14 ##@##..########L######\n1191\t 15 ##<############>######\n1192\t 16 ######################\n1193\t```\n1194\t\n1195\t**Areas:**\n1196\t\n1197\t| Area | Cells |\n1198\t|---|---|\n1199\t| Wardens' Walk | (2,9 – 2,14) |\n1200\t| Wardens' Post (safe room) | (5..6, 12..14) |"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c642ce04-34f8-46f2-be98-ceed51703e52","uuid":"830c4645-823b-465d-bf2a-d2b82deaf38e","timestamp":"2026-11-04T03:26:33.283Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium.build__20261103-202616__x53986f/work/PLAN.md","content":"  - **Bottom:** `HP 11/11 · Defense 14 · Lv 2 Fighter · XP 140/250 · Food ███░`.\n  - **Actions:** ✕ takes or places (it carries the item into the Hand, or swaps), □ Use, △ Drop at your feet, R2 Sheet. ○ returns a carried item, then closes the screen.\n  - **The Sheet tab** shows the stats and their modifiers, class abilities, resistances and the spellbook or the prayers. Dismiss (NPCs) is here, behind a confirm.\n- **Cast.** Opened by a caster's book or symbol hand.\n  - A centred panel of about 260×150, with level tabs L1, L2, L3 (shoulders switch them).\n  - Rows read \"Spark Dart ×2\", with a description and the target type.\n  - ✕ casts. A `member` target then moves the highlight across the cards (◀ ▶, ✕). A `line`, `front`, `door` or `party` spell fires at once. ○ cancels.\n- **Camp (L3, C).** The view darkens and a small campfire light glows in the cell. Tiles in 2 rows of 5 (§4.9).\n  - **Rest** shows a rest panel: the hours counting, HP ticking up on the cards and ○ Stop.\n  - **Memorize** and **Pray**: known spells on the left (grouped by level, with descriptions) and slots on the right. ✕ on a spell fills the next free slot of its level, ✕ on a slot empties it, △ \"Same as before\".\n  - **Scribe**: scrolls in the party's packs that the mage doesn't know; ✕ learns one.\n  - **Formation**: the 2×3 places; ✕ twice swaps two members.\n  - **Eat**: a confirm, then a summary of who ate what.\n  - **Save** and **Load** open the engine's slot screens (`saves.show`).\n  - **Settings** opens `game.menu('settings')`.\n- **Map (Create, M).**\n  - A parchment-coloured panel with the floor's explored cells at 8 to 10 px per cell, and a legend row at the bottom.\n  - L1 and R1 switch between visited floors; the d-pad or stick pans a map larger than the screen; ○ closes.\n  - Dev *reveal* shows everything.\n- **Journal (J, or the tab from Party or Map).** Quests, Notes, Deeds and Log. Notes open the **Reader**, a parchment page with the note's text at the normal size, paged with the d-pad.\n- **Dialogue.** `E.Dialog` at the bottom: portrait on the left, name in brass and 3 lines a page. ✕ finishes the line, then turns the page; ○ fast-forwards; choices are a vertical list.\n- **Title.**\n  - **The view.** The Drain-gate stage from the intro (§7.3, stage B) at night. The camera pushes slowly toward the grate, the torches flicker, and every 12 s the great bolt slides home with a shake and a thud.\n  - **The logo.** **EYE OF THE BOLT-HOLDER** in `E.font.title`, scale 4, brass colours (§5.1), with a slow glint across it, and \"A thousand locks. One eye.\" under it.\n  - **The menu,** a centred `E.Menu`: Continue (only when a save exists), New Game, Load Game, Rat Run, Settings, About & Credits.\n  - **The bottom line:** the prompts for the last device and the version (`E.versionLabel()`, plus the game's own version).\n  - **Music:** `title`.\n  - **The attract mode** starts after 10 s idle (§9). The touch notice is shown on touch-only devices (§5.7).\n- **Creation:** §4.4. **The floor card:** §4.1. **About and Credits:** §11. **Touch notice:** §5.7.\n- **Game over.** \"THE PARTY IS LOST\" in the title font over the frozen, darkened view; one line from the floor (\"The Drains keep what they take.\"); then Load last save · Load game · Title.\n- **Ending.** The ending cutscene (§7.3), then the credits roll (the §11 Credits page, scrolling), then the stats panel (time, kills, secrets 3, deeds 3, deaths, levels) and Title. The `ending` song plays.\n\n### 5.4 Focus navigation and the mouse\n\n- **One focus system** (`61-ui-kit.js`) for every screen.\n  - Each screen registers its widgets as rects with an id, an action and optional explicit neighbours.\n  - The d-pad and the left stick (menus use the engine's `up/down/left/right`, which include the stick) move to the nearest widget in that direction, by geometry; explicit neighbours override.\n  - Holding a direction repeats (`input.repeat`, 0.35 s, then 0.1 s).\n- **The mouse.**\n  - Moving the pointer over a widget focuses it; a left click acts as ✕; a right click on a slot acts as □; the wheel scrolls lists.\n  - Party screen drag and drop: mouse-down carries the item, mouse-up places it.\n- **Mouse in the 3D view.** Each frame, project the interactables in front with `world.project`: the front wall's feature, the items in the front and own cells, doors, the monsters in front and alcoves. Each gets a screen hotspot.\n  - Hovering one outlines it (a soft brass rim drawn with the pen around the thing) and shows a tooltip, e.g. \"Lever — click to pull\".\n  - A left click on a hotspot uses it. With an item in the Hand, a left click on the lower view puts it down and a left click on the upper view throws it, as in the source.\n  - A right click anywhere in the view is **Party Strike**.\n- **Party cards.** A click on a hand slot uses that hand (the source's core gesture); a click on a portrait selects; a right click on a portrait opens that member in the Party screen.\n\n### 5.5 Prompts and glyphs\n\n- **One painter, `glyph(g, x, y, action)`**, draws a badge for the action's binding on the last device:\n\n  | Device | Badge |\n  |---|---|\n  | Pad, PlayStation (default) | ✕ blue, ○ red, □ pink, △ green, drawn as shapes on a dark disc; L1, R1, L2, R2, L3, R3, Options and Create as rounded labels; D-pad and stick icons |\n  | Pad, Xbox (Settings → Controls → Button symbols) | A green, B red, X blue, Y yellow letters; LB, RB, LT, RT, View, Menu |\n  | Keyboard | a keycap with the bound key (`input.codeLabel`) |\n  | Mouse | a mouse icon with the left or right button lit |\n\n  Never print raw codes. Build every prompt string from `input.label(action)` through the painter, so rebinding just works.\n- **When the prompts change.** They switch the moment `lastDevice` changes: a pad button or a stick past the dead zone, a key, or a mouse move of more than 4 px or a click.\n\n### 5.6 Input map (all rebindable except the menu actions)\n\n| Action | Gamepad (standard mapping) | Keyboard | Mouse |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Step forward / back | Left stick ↑ ↓, D-pad ↑ ↓ | W / S, ↑ / ↓, Numpad 8 / 5 or 2 | — |\n| Strafe left / right | Left stick ← → | A / D, Numpad 4 / 6 | — |\n| Turn left / right | D-pad ← →, right stick ← → (a flick, repeating every 0.35 s while held) | Q / E, ← / →, Numpad 7 / 9 | — |\n| Use / interact / take / place / stow | ✕ (tap) | F | left click on a thing in the view |\n| Put the Hand's item down | ✕ (hold 0.4 s) | H | left click on the lower view |\n| Throw the Hand's item | ○ | G | left click on the upper view |\n| Party Strike | □ | Space | right click in the view |\n| Select member previous / next | L1 / R1 | Tab / Shift+Tab, or 1–6 | click a portrait |\n| Selected member's main / off hand | R2 / L2 | 1–6 main hand (and select); Shift+1–6 off hand | click a hand slot |\n| Party screen | △ | I | portrait right click, HUD icon |\n| Camp | L3 | C | HUD icon |\n| Examine ahead | R3 | X | middle click |\n| Automap | Create (acts on release; ignored when Options was pressed while Create was held) | M | HUD icon |\n| Journal | (from the Party or Map tabs, or the pause menu) | J | HUD icon |\n| Pause menu | Options | Esc, P | the engine's corner button |\n| Menus | D-pad / stick, ✕ confirm, ○ back, L1 / R1 tabs | arrows, Enter, Backspace or Esc | hover, click, wheel |\n\n**Implementation notes.**\n- Define your own play actions (`fwd, back, strafeL, strafeR, turnL, turnR, use, strike, selPrev, selNext, handMain, handOff, party, camp, examine, map, journal, throw, putDown`) in the play scene's `input` map, as the kit did.\n- **Don't use the engine's merged `left/right` in play**: they merge the d-pad and the stick, and here they mean different things.\n  - Read the left stick from `input.padAxes[0]` and `[1]`, with the dead zone and a 0.5 threshold, for move and strafe.\n  - Read the right stick X from `padAxes[2]`, as a flick with re-arm, for turning.\n  - The d-pad codes are `Pad12` to `Pad15`.\n- **Hub rule.** While Create (`Pad8`) is held, ignore Options (`Pad9`), and don't toggle the map on Create's release if Options went down in between.\n- **Idle detection** (attract mode): any action pressed, any `input.held` code, a stick past 0.3, a pointer move over 4 px or a click.\n\n### 5.7 Touch-only devices\n\n- **Detection.** `matchMedia('(pointer: coarse)')` with no `(hover: hover)`, and no keyboard or gamepad input seen yet. On such devices `input.touchEnabled = false`: no touch buttons and no stick.\n- **The title** shows a panel: \"**Controller or keyboard required.** Connect a controller or a keyboard to play.\" The engine's top-right menu button stays and opens Settings.\n- **The attract mode runs** after the same 10 s idle. A touch exits it to the title, which shows the notice again.\n- **The notice hides** the moment a key or a pad button arrives, and play works normally from then on.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Presentation: art, animation and audio\n\n### 6.1 Art direction\n\n- **The base is the engine's native 3D look,** the one the spike showed: code-drawn textures, `world.res = 'pixels'` (chunky low-res pixels), toon light, outlines on, characters as **cards** (`world.look = 'card'`: the rigs drawn as pixel art from the camera's own angle) and fog for the source's distance falloff.\n- **Lighting.** `torchShadows: 2`, `torchLights: 6`, the party's lantern as a `world.light` at the eyes, and `glowLights: 4` for spells.\n- **New art** wherever the source's feel needs it: wall features, doors, floor items, the creatures in §6.3, the boss, the brass UI, item icons and the stages for the title and the cutscenes.\n- **Props.** For generic set dressing (bones, barrels, crates, chains, cobwebs, banners, candles, tables), search the store first with `node tools/asset-find.mjs \"bones\"`, using `kaykit-dungeon-remastered`, `kenney-mini-dungeon` and `kenney-graveyard`. Cut a set with `tools/asset-set.mjs`, load it with `E.addAssets`, and place props with `world.shape(id, …)` or `{ shape }` in the legend.\n\n| Floor | Ground (`level.ground`, `colors`) | Walls (`side`, `color`) | Fog | Ambient `[sky, ground, power]` | Signature dressing |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 The Hasp Drains | flagstone `#3e4a44 / #2a332f / #55615a`; a floor colour function paints dark-green **water channels** (6 units wide) down the Rat Channel and Cistern cells | brick `#4a5048` | `#06080a`, 24 → 150 | `#4a5a5a, #1a201e, 2.6` | floor drains (grates), dripping pipes (pen tubes), slime streaks, rusty chains, rat bones, sluice wheels |\n| 2 The Tumbler Halls | tiles `#5a4a3a / #3e3228 / #7a6450` | block `#6a5a48` | `#0a0806`, 40 → 220 | `#7a6048, #2a2018, 3.0` | turning **wall gears** (pen rings of teeth, slowly rotating), anvils, workbenches, cogs on the floor, forge glow (orange lights) in the Workshop |\n| 3 The Gloam Deeps | plain `#2a2434 / #1a1622 / #3a3248` | block `#2e2838` | `#040306`, 20 → 130 | `#3a3a5a, #141220, 2.2` | carved **eye reliefs** on walls (pen), shut-eye banners, bone piles, pale blue candles in the Chapel (lights) |\n| 4 The Eye's Vault | tiles `#3a3e46`; the arena floor colour function adds faint cyan rune lines | block `#30343c` | `#020204`, 30 → 200 | `#2a3040, #0c0e14, 2.0` | the boss's amber light, cyan lightning flashes, the 3 Great Locks' rune lights going out as they turn |\n\n- **Item icons.** Make about 60 of them as `E.sprite` strings, designed at 12×12 and drawn at ×1 on the cards and ×2 in the Party screen. Shade them with `E.tones`.\n- **Item models.** Each floor item also gets a tiny **3D model drawn with the pen**, lying flat at its quadrant spot:\n  - blade (sword, dagger): a thin box with a cross-guard;\n  - axe or mace: a head on a haft;\n  - crossbow; bolts or arrows: thin tubes;\n  - potion: a ball and a neck, in its colour;\n  - scroll: a tube; book: a box;\n  - key: a ring plus a shaft with teeth, in the key's colour;\n  - rock: a grey lump of balls; ration: a wrapped box;\n  - gear: a ring of boxes; ward: a toothed disc.\n\n### 6.2 The 3D presenter (`40–44`)\n\n- **Building a floor.**\n  - Map each cell to 2×2 level tiles (`#` → `##`, open → `..`). A torch wall feature turns the tile on its open side into `t`, the kit's NICHE trick.\n  - Make `new E.World3D(game, { level, look: 'card', res: 'pixels', torchLights: 6, torchShadows: 2, torchPower: 18, ambient, fog, sky: fogColour, camera: { mode: 'fixed' }, overlay: { fov: 60 }, onDraw })`.\n  - Create all of the floor's lights at build time (lantern, candles, forge glows, the boss), as the engine requires.\n  - Build every floor's world at boot and `prepare()` it, so a floor change never compiles a shader mid-game. On a floor change, swap the active world.\n- **Each frame,** from the sim state:\n  - **Camera:** `world.camera.fixed = { x, y, z: EYE + bob, yaw, pitch: −0.04, fov: 74 }`, from the party's tween (the kit's `place()`). A bump adds the lurch, a hit adds `game.shake`, a pit fall drops z by 40 and fades.\n  - **Doors and gates:** `world.thing('door', …, { w: 32, h: 46, swing })`; set `t.open` toward the sim's state and call `world.setSolid` when it opens.\n  - **Secret walls** (and **illusory walls**): a movable wall block that is **indistinguishable from the level's walls**. Try `world.box({ fixed: true, side: <the floor's side style>, color })` first; if it doesn't match, add a `wallBlock` helper to the 3D engine that reuses the level's wall material (risk 3, §13). A secret block sinks into the floor when opened; an illusory one never moves (the party's step through it is masked by the dissolve).\n  - **Wall features:** custom `E.World3D.THINGS`, drawn with the pen on the wall face (local +y out of the wall, as the kit's `wallLever`).\n\n    | THING | How to draw it |\n    |---|---|\n    | `wallLever` | the kit's |\n    | `wallButton` | a square stone and a brass boss that presses in |\n    | `catch` | a slightly proud stone with a crack, or a brass rivet plate; glints under Seeing |\n    | `alcove` | a dark recessed box that draws its items inside |\n    | `keyhole` | per key shape: iron round, warded cross, gear toothed, bone skull, ward discs |\n    | `plaque` | a stone tablet with dark glyph dashes |\n    | `grate`, `pipe`, `chain`, `gearWall` (rotating), `eyeRelief` | decor |\n    | `candle` | a holder, a wax stick and a flame glow when lit, paired with its light |\n    | `greatLock` | a big wheel with rune glow, spun over 2 s |\n    | `undergate` | a great door with 3 keyholes and 7 bolt bars that slide when a ward goes in |\n    | `cage` | bars |\n    | `shrine` | a ring of tiny rat statues |\n    | `clockFace` | a dial with 4 gear sockets and hands that move once the clock is whole |\n    | `altarSlab` | a floor slab |\n    | `stairs` | the kit's `stair` (down), plus `stairUp` |\n    | `pitEdge` | a dark hole with a lip; a bridge slab when bridged |\n    | `plate` | the kit's |\n    | `teleporterField` | a soft swirl glow, only when not silent |\n\n  - **Floor items:** pen models at the quadrant spots of the visible cells (`onDraw`).\n  - **Monsters:** cards (`world.mob` with `rig`, `blob` or `orb`) are steered toward their slot's position with `vx`/`vy` as the kit does (`fly: true` for fliers). Their `anim` comes from the sim: attack phase, hurt flash, `die` pose, sink. Pen-drawn creatures are drawn in `onDraw` from their sim state and a local animation clock (§6.3).\n  - **Projectiles and FX:** `world.glow` for bolts and orbs, pen bars for lightning, `game.particles` for sparks, embers, smoke and damage `text`, and `world.arc` for floor telegraphs (Bolt Rain).\n  - **First-person overlay:** with `world.overlay.pen`, draw the striking member's weapon swinging across its side of the view: left for places 1, 3 and 5, right for 2, 4 and 6. The crossbow rises and kicks; a caster's hand glows in the spell's colour.\n  - **Hover outlines and name tags:** project with `world.project`, then draw them in the HUD.\n- **NullView** implements the same interface (`enter(floor)`, `frame(r)`, `event(e)`, `pick(sx, sy)`) as no-ops for Node.\n\n### 6.3 Creature recipes\n\nThe sizes follow the engine's guidance (heroes `size` 1.2 to 1.4, bosses larger). Every rig gets a real palette.\n\n| Creature | Build | Recipe | Animation notes |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Drain Rat | card, `E.Blob` | `{ R: 3.6, ears: 'cat', tail: true, feet: true, mouth: 'fangs', colors: { base: '#6a5a50', dk: '#3e342e', lt: '#9a8a7a', eye: '#ff6a4a' } }` | fast squash scurry; the wind-up is a rear-back squash |\n| Bloat Leech | pen | 5 balls (r 4 → 2.5) along a sine curve on the floor, `#b89a9a` with `#7a5a5a` rings; a mouth ring of 6 small balls; a wet glint | the body undulates; it lunges out 6 units on the strike |\n| Latchkin | card, `E.Humanoid` | `{ size: .85, build: 'chibi', hunch: .5, hood: true, outfit: 'tunic', bladeLen: 5, eyeGlow: '#ffd24a', colors: { skin: '#7a8a5a', hair: '#4a3a2a', cloth: '#6a4a32', pants: '#3a2e22', metal: '#9a9aa8' } }`, plus a pen ring of keys at the belt | the `thrust` move; it stays in a crouch-run while fleeing |\n| Drain Ooze | card, `E.Blob` | `{ R: 8, face: 'front', mouth: true, colors: { base: '#5a8a3a', dk: '#2e5a22', lt: '#9ad06a', spec: '#e8ffd0' } }` | a slow wobble; it slams by squashing down; it splashes green particles |\n| Rat Knot | pen | 6 rat-body balls in a ring with ear cones, tails as tubes knotted at the middle | the ring wobbles and turns; two bites a strike |\n| Snick, the Latch-Boss | card, `E.Humanoid` | `{ size: 1.0, build: 'bulky', hunch: .3, hat: { style: 'crown', color: '#c8a040' }, armor: true, outfit: 'coat', bladeLen: 9, eyeGlow: '#ffd24a', colors: { skin: '#7a8a5a', cloth: '#5a3a2a', plate: '#a08040' } }`, plus a pen cape of hanging keys | the `overhead` move; it rattles its keys at 50% when it calls for help |\n| Tinker Skeleton | card, `E.Humanoid` | `{ size: 1.2, build: 'skeleton', outfit: 'coat', bladeLen: 7, colors: { bone: '#d8cfb4', cloth: '#5a4030', metal: '#8a8a90' } }`, plus a pen hammer head on the blade | the `overhead` and `slash` moves; it collapses into bones on death |\n| Rustling | card, `E.Blob` | `{ R: 4.2, horns: true, feet: true, mouth: true, colors: { base: '#b8642a', dk: '#7a3a18', lt: '#e8a060' } }` | the horns twitch; it throws rust-flake particles when it hits |\n| Brass Spider | pen | abdomen ball r 7 and cephalothorax r 4.5 in `#b8923a`; 8 legs of 2 tubes each with procedural tetrapod gait (sine phase lifts); 4 red eye glows | legs step; it lunges on the strike; it falls apart into parts on death |\n| Clockwork Sentinel | card, `E.Humanoid` | `{ size: 1.6, build: 'bulky', armor: true, hat: { style: 'helmet', color: '#8a6a3a' }, bladeLen: 14, eyeGlow: '#ff8a3a', colors: { cloth: '#6a4a2a', plate: '#b08a4a', metal: '#c8a868', skin: '#5a4a3a' } }`, plus a pen wind-up key turning on its back | the `twohand` move with a 0.8 s wind-up; the key spins faster during it |\n| Lidless Hound | pen | a quadruped (adapt the 3D horror kit's dogs, `src/starter3d/40-horror.js`): pale `#c8b8b0`, smooth eyeless head, long jaw | run, leap and bite |\n| Gloam Seer | card, `E.Humanoid` | `{ size: 1.25, build: 'heroic', outfit: 'robe', hood: true, weapon: 'staff', eyeGlow: '#8ae0ff', colors: { cloth: '#d8d0e8', hair: '#3a2a4a', skin: '#b8b0c8', trim: '#6a4a9a' } }`, plus an eye-sigil glow over the staff | the `cast` pose while charging a Locking Bolt (cyan glow growing) |\n| Gloam Warden | card, `E.Humanoid` | `{ size: 1.35, build: 'heroic', armor: true, hat: { style: 'helmet', color: '#2a2434' }, weapon: 'staff', eyeGlow: '#e8e8ff', colors: { cloth: '#2a2434', plate: '#4a4458', metal: '#9a98a8', skin: '#b8b0c8' } }`, plus a pen halberd blade on the staff | the `thrust` move (reaches two cells) |\n| Gazer | card orb plus pen | an orb `{ color: '#e8a040', r: 4 }`; pen iris (a flattened ball `#3a8a6a`), pupil, two lid slabs, 3 fin cones | blinks; the pupil tracks the party; it glows before Spark Gaze |\n| Lockjaw Golem | card, `E.Humanoid` | `{ size: 1.9, build: 'bulky', armor: true, weapon: null, eyeGlow: '#7ad8ff', colors: { cloth: '#3a3e46', plate: '#5a606a', skin: '#4a4e56' } }`, plus a pen **padlock head** (box body and shackle tube) instead of a hat | the `haymaker` move; heavy footstep shakes |\n| **The Bolt-Holder** | pen | an eye ball r 14 (sclera `#e8e0c8` with red vein bars); a flattened amber iris r 7 (`#e8a030`) facing the party; a black pupil r 3.5 that dilates; upper and lower lid slabs that blink and narrow for the Gaze; **7 radial iron bolts** (bars 22 long and 2.5 thick, with 5×5×3 heads) that slide out 2 per Great Lock (the 7th, the keystone, never moves); cyan lightning arcs (jagged pen bars) between neighbouring bolt heads; a ±3 bob; an amber `world.light`; red tint and crack lines in phase 3 | it must not read as a beholder: no eyestalks, no mouth, no tentacles. It reads as a caged iron lantern-eye. |\n| Ghosts (race) | card, `E.Humanoid` | a hooded cloak in the player's seat colour, `fade 0.45`, a lantern glow in the seat colour, and the hub name as a HUD tag | they glide between the cells they report |\n\n**People** (portraits and cutscenes):\n- the party (§7.9);\n- Keywarden Imelda Strake: heroic, band crown, coat, navy and silver;\n- Magister Abel Lintel: robe, pointed hat, long white hair;\n- Ysolde Vane: robe, long hair, ghost blue, drawn translucent;\n- Tamsin: size 0.9, ponytail, green hood;\n- Durgan: bulky, braided beard, iron helmet;\n- Veil: robe, hood, eyes shut (draw them closed).\n\n### 6.4 Animation list (new, on the engine's rigs, tweens and pen)\n\n- **Party view.** Step glide with bob; turn ease; bump lurch; pit fall (drop and fade); teleport (a cut or a swirl); spinner (a short wobble only when *visible*: none for silent spinners); hit shake; level-up glow on the card; KO slump (the portrait tinted grey); death toll (the card turns to bones); first-person weapon swings for each weapon family (blade, axe, blunt, spear thrust, crossbow, bow, sling, throw, punch); casting hand glows.\n- **World.** Gates rising with a chain rattle and wooden doors swinging; levers flipping and buttons and catches pressing in; plates sinking; secret walls sinking; the trapdoor dropping open; the pit bridge rising; teleporter swirl; gears turning; candles lighting and guttering; the Great Locks spinning; the Undergate's 7 bolts drawing back one by one; the clock's hands moving once it is whole; the boss's bolts sliding, lids blinking, iris dilating and lightning arcing.\n- **Monsters.** Idle, move glide, wind-up telegraph (the move's `wind` phase, at least 0.5 s), strike, hurt flash and recoil, death (the `die` pose, then sink; blobs squash flat; constructs fall apart into pen parts; the leech curls).\n- **UI.** Cooldown wipes; damage pops; card shake; chevrons; focus pulse; toast slides; the title logo shimmer.\n\n### 6.5 Audio: code only, no files\n\n- **The music director.** It plays a song per floor through `game.audio.music(song, { fade: 1 })`. Every dungeon song carries a `fight` track (drums and bass, `on: false`) that comes in with `audio.layer('fight', 1, .5)` when any monster engages and goes out 4 s after the last one. Stings use `audio.sting`. All songs are original, in the step-sequencer format (`{ bpm, steps, tracks: [{ wave, vol, notes }] }`).\n\n  | Song | Feel | Seed motif (original) |\n  |---|---|---|\n  | `title`, \"The City of a Thousand Locks\" | 76 bpm, D minor, bell pulses over a low triangle | `D4 - F4 A4 G4 - F4 E4 \\| D4 - - - C4 E4 G4 F4 \\| E4 - D4 C#4 D4 - - -` |\n  | `drains` | 60 bpm, a sparse drone, a lonely pulse every 8 bars, drips as sfx | low `A1` drone; a `pulse25` figure `A3 . C4 . E4 . . . \\| D4 . C4 . B3 . . .` |\n  | `tumbler` | 96 bpm in 6/8, ticking percussion | `drums` `h . h c . h` over `E2 . B2 E2 . B2` |\n  | `gloam` | 54 bpm, sine pads, a tritone colour | `C3` plus `F#3` pads, a choir-like sine line in long notes |\n  | `vault` / `boss` | 138 bpm, saw bass, lightning arpeggios | `A2 A2 . A2 C3 . A2 . \\| G2 G2 . G2 Bb2 . G2 .`, arps `A4 E5 A5 E5` |\n  | `camp` | 70 bpm, a lullaby | the title motif in a major key, triangle |\n  | `ending` | 84 bpm, D major | the title motif resolved |\n  | stings | — | `levelUp`, `deed`, `secret`, `wardFound`, `gameOver`, `victory`, `npcJoin` |\n\n- **Sound effects** (`audio.define`, the engine's voice format; the kit's `SOUNDS` are the template). Define every one of these:\n  - steps per floor: wet stone, metal grating, dust, stone;\n  - turn, bump, door open and close, gate grind, lever clank, button click, catch click, plate thunk, secret-wall grind, illusion shimmer, trapdoor, fall and land;\n  - teleporter whoosh (visible ones only), spinner grind, dart volley;\n  - key turn, lock fail, lockpick scratch and snap, alcove place and take;\n  - item pickup, drop and throw whoosh, land clatter, eat crunch, drink glug, scroll unroll, wand zap;\n  - swings (blade, axe, blunt), crossbow and bow twangs, sling whirr;\n  - hits (flesh, metal, bone, ooze), miss whiff, crit clang, party hurt;\n  - level up, death toll, raise;\n  - each spell: cast, travel loop and impact;\n  - monster voices for each type (squeak, slurp, chitter, rattle, clank, growl, chant, gaze hum);\n  - boss: roar, lightning crack, bolt slam, lock turn and shriek;\n  - UI: move, confirm, back, error, tab;\n  - ambience loops per floor: drips, distant gears, whispers, a low hum.\n\n  Pan by bearing with the patched `{ pan }` (§3.9).\n- **Voices: the babble synth** (`50-audio.js`, on `game.audio.ctx` and routed to the voice bus).\n  - **Per-speaker profile:** `{ base: Hz, range: semitones, rate: syllables/s, wave, formant: ×, breath: 0..1, vib: [Hz, depth], echo: 0..1 }`. The profiles:\n\n    | Speaker | base Hz | range | rate | wave | other |\n    |---|---|---|---|---|---|\n    | Narrator | 95 | 3 | 9 | triangle | echo 0.2 |\n    | Keywarden | 170 | 4 | 12 | square | |\n    | Lintel | 120 | 5 | 10 | saw | |\n    | Tamsin | 300 | 7 | 15 | pulse | |\n    | Durgan | 105 | 4 | 11 | square | |\n    | Ysolde | 220 | 5 | 9 | sine | echo 0.4 |\n    | Veil | 240 | 3 | 10 | triangle | breath 0.5 |\n    | Snick | 260 | 8 | 16 | square | |\n    | Bolt-Holder | 70 | 6 | 8 | saw | ring mod 30 Hz, echo 0.5 |\n\n    The party members also get profiles from their race and sex.\n  - **Driving it.** Set `talk.voice = null`. Each update, read `talk.shown`; for every two new letters (and on every vowel), emit a syllable.\n  - **The syllable:**\n    - The vowel picks a formant pair (F1/F2): a 800/1200, e 400/2000, i 300/2300, o 450/800, u 325/700, × `formant`.\n    - The letter's code picks the pitch inside `range`, so a word always sounds the same.\n    - Plosives (b d g k p t) add a 10 ms noise click; fricatives (f s v z h) add a 40 ms high-passed noise; nasals (m n) add a low hum.\n    - `?` rises at the end, `!` is louder and higher, `.` pauses 0.15 s and `,` pauses 0.08 s.\n  - **The voice:** an oscillator into two parallel band-pass filters (Q 8) into a gain envelope (5 ms attack, 0.6× hold, 30 ms release), then the bus.\n  - **Barks:** short babble for party pain (\"Oof!\"), effort (\"Hah!\"), level-up (\"Yes!\") and casting, and for monster taunts.\n  - **Test it in Node.** `babble.plan(text, profile)` returns syllable events (time, pitch, F1, F2, noise) and must be deterministic (§14). In Node there is no AudioContext, so the synth is a no-op.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Content\n\n### 7.1 World bible (all original)\n\n- **Hasp, the City of a Thousand Locks.** A walled river port that grew rich on locks. Its sigil is a key crossed with a bolt. It is ruled by the **Council of Keys** under **High Keywarden Imelda Strake**, stern and practical. The city's wizard is **Magister Abel Lintel**, dry, old and worried.\n- **The Tumblerwrights' Guild.** The finest locksmiths in the world. Their halls sat under the city until a disaster sealed them a century ago. Their last guildmistress, **Ysolde Vane**, haunts the halls.\n- **The Undergate.** The guild's masterwork: a gate beneath the city's foundations that seals something older, which this demo only hints at. To watch it, the guild forged **the Watcher**, an eye that never closes, and gave it **seven Great Bolts** to hold. The Watcher learned to love holding. It now calls itself **the Bolt-Holder** and turns the locks of Hasp from below: \"Every lock is a promise. I keep them all.\"\n- **Its servants.**\n  - **Latchkins**: small sewer goblins who worship keys and steal iron. Their chief is **Snick, the Latch-Boss**.\n  - The guild's own clockwork and its dead workers, wound up again.\n  - The **Gloam-folk** of the deep, pale people who believe the Eye is a god and call themselves the **Lidless**: their Seers, Wardens and hounds.\n- **The quest.** Gather the **Three Wards** (copper from the Drains, brass from the Guild Vault, iron from the Lidless Reliquary), open the Undergate and close the Eye.\n- **The humour.** The title is playful; the prose is earnest. Wit comes in small doses: Tamsin's quips, dry item descriptions, the Rat King's crown.\n\n### 7.2 Writing style guide\n\nThe model is the source's voice: terse, second-person, past the fourth wall never.\n\n- **Messages** are one short sentence, present tense, addressed to \"you\" or naming a member. Use plain words and full stops; keep exclamation marks for danger and wonder.\n  - \"You hear a click in the distance.\"\n  - \"There is a loose stone here.\"\n  - \"The bolt will not move.\"\n  - \"This key does not fit.\"\n  - \"The Iron Key turns. The door opens.\"\n  - \"A hidden door grinds open!\"\n  - \"The wall is an illusion!\"\n  - \"The floor gives way!\"\n  - \"You feel a twisting underfoot.\"\n  - \"Nothing happens.\"\n  - \"Darts fly from the walls!\"\n  - \"Cobb is hungry.\"\n  - \"Odelia is poisoned!\"\n  - \"Brannoc swings at the air.\"\n  - \"The Drain Rat dies.\"\n  - \"You may not rest with enemies near.\"\n  - \"You are awakened by something moving!\"\n  - \"A hidden deed is done!\"\n  - \"Ysa has reached level 3!\"\n- **Inscriptions** are in CAPITALS, formal and a little archaic: \"NOT EVERY STONE IS STONE.\"\n- **Narration** (intro and ending) is stately, in the third person, with short paragraphs and one image each.\n- **NPCs** speak formally but each in their own voice:\n  - Tamsin: quick and cheeky.\n  - Durgan: gruff and practical.\n  - Ysolde: sorrowful and old-fashioned.\n  - Veil: hushed and strange, always talking about eyes.\n  - The Bolt-Holder: grand, slow, with CAPITALS for its emphasis.\n- **Item descriptions** are 1 to 2 dry sentences: \"It has seen better days, and better locks.\"\n- **Never** use modern slang, game-mechanic jargon in the fiction (say \"slots\" only in menus), or the source's names.\n\n### 7.3 Story beats and cutscenes\n\nThe cutscenes are 3D stages, small `E.World3D` sets built at boot, with rigs, a camera moved by `game.script` and `game.tween`, dialogue boxes, babble voices and stings. Any button speeds the text; holding Options or Esc for 1 s skips the cutscene.\n\n**INTRO** (about 75 s):\n- *Stage A*, the Council Hall at night: pillars, banners, two braziers, a long table, Strake and Lintel.\n- *Stage B*, the Drain-gate: a stair down into the dark, a grate, and the party's four rigs.\n\n1. NARRATOR: \"Hasp. The city of a thousand locks.\"\n2. NARRATOR: \"For three hundred years its Tumblerwrights forged the finest locks in the world, and its people slept soundly behind them.\"\n3. NARRATOR: \"Then the locks began to turn by themselves.\"\n4. STRAKE: \"Doors bolt themselves in empty houses. Wells cap shut. Last night the east granary locked forty men inside and would not open for axes.\"\n5. LINTEL: \"It comes from below. Past the Drains, past the old guild halls… from the Undergate itself.\"\n6. STRAKE: \"You were recommended to me as people who open things. Go down. Find what holds our bolts, and break its grip.\"\n7. *(Stage B)* NARRATOR: \"The Drain-gate groans open. You step down into the dark.\"\n8. NARRATOR: \"Behind you, the grate crashes shut. A great bolt slides home with a sound like a closing tomb.\"\n   - The camera shakes, a pen-drawn bolt slides across the grate, and the torches gutter.\n9. NARRATOR: \"Somewhere far below, something blinks.\"\n   - Cut to black. An amber eye opens for 0.5 s, with the boss's hum.\n10. Play begins on floor 1 with the log line \"The grate above is bolted fast. There is no way back.\"\n\n**Mid-game beats** (in-dungeon, through E.Story):\n- Tamsin freed (floor 1).\n- Snick's barks.\n- Ysolde's ghost twice (floor 2).\n- Durgan (floor 2).\n- Veil's choice (floor 3).\n- The Undergate opening (floor 3, a 10 s in-engine moment: the camera holds, seven bolts draw back one by one, a deep chord).\n- The Bolt-Holder's taunts (floor 4).\n\n**ENDING** (about 60 s):\n- *Stage C*, the Vault after the battle: light pours from the cracked Eye.\n- *Stage D*, the city square at dawn: houses, doors swinging open, Strake, Lintel and the party.\n\n1. NARRATOR: \"The Eye cracks from lid to lid, and its light goes out.\"\n2. NARRATOR: \"One by one, the seven Great Bolts fall silent.\"\n3. *(Stage D)* NARRATOR: \"Above, in the city of a thousand locks, every door swings open at once.\"\n4. STRAKE: \"Hasp is in your debt. The guild's last forge will cast your names into the Undergate itself.\"\n5. LINTEL: \"Yet the Undergate was built to keep something in. With its Watcher gone…\"\n6. NARRATOR: \"Far beneath the city, in a darkness older than locks, something tries the door.\"\n7. Title card **THE END**, then the credits roll (§11), then the stats: time, kills, secrets found out of 3, hidden deeds out of 3, deaths and the party's levels. Back to the title.\n\n### 7.4 The floors\n\n- **Legend** (one character per cell):\n\n  | Char | Meaning |\n  |---|---|\n  | `#` | wall |\n  | `.` | floor |\n  | `@` | start or arrival |\n  | `<` `>` | stairs |\n  | `+` | wooden door |\n  | `=` | gate |\n  | `L` `K` | locked door |\n  | `M` | magic seal |\n  | `H` | secret wall |\n  | `I` | illusory wall |\n  | `P` | plate |\n  | `T` | dart trap |\n  | `O` | pit |\n  | `o` | trapdoor |\n  | `^` | teleporter |\n  | `S` | spinner |\n  | `U` | the Undergate |\n  | `*` | pit landing |\n  | `B` | the boss |\n\n- **Coordinates** are (x, y) with y = 0 at the top; the rulers above each map give x.\n- **Wall features** are given as *(stand x, y, face)*.\n- **Checked during planning:** every walkthrough below was checked with a reachability script (each target reachable with only the doors opened so far, and every gated area unreachable before its gate). It came to 157 checks, including both of Veil's branches and the Sump. Your content lint repeats them (§14).\n\n#### 7.4.1 Floor 1: The Hasp Drains (22×17)\n\n*\"Cold water talks to itself in the channels. The walls sweat.\"* (floor card)\n\n```\n    0000000000111111111122\n    0123456789012345678901\n  0 ######################\n  1 #.....=.#####........#\n  2 #.....#######........#\n  3 ##+#####.########L####\n  4 ##.#####H########.####\n  5 #....###.....####.####\n  6 #....###......P.=.####\n  7 #............#########\n  8 #....###.....#########\n  9 ##.######I##.#########\n 10 ##=#####...#...T....##\n 11 ##.#####...########=##\n 12 ##.##..#...###.......#\n 13 ##..+..#######.......#\n 14 ##@##..########L######\n 15 ##<############>######\n 16 ######################\n```\n\n**Areas:**\n\n| Area | Cells |\n|---|---|\n| Wardens' Walk | (2,9 – 2,14) |\n| Wardens' Post (safe room) | (5..6, 12..14) |","numLines":420,"startLine":781,"totalLines":2145}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01CJG8VyaUDv9TT7vZJ3BBxW","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
