s not built. A solo Rat Run with a best-run ghost is not built either.\",\n    \"testing\": \"node tests/run.mjs: lint of the maps and wiring, sim determinism and save round-trip, the walkthrough bot clearing floor 1 and reaching floor 2, and a browser smoke test opening the bundle from file://. Floors 3 and 4 are not cleared by the bot.\",\n    \"research\": \"Read the engine's API card, its 3D manual and the starter crawler kit; no web research\",\n    \"environment\": \"Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux (WSL2); browser: headless Chromium 1243 via Playwright\",\n    \"model\": \"Anthropic, claude-haiku-5-5, reasoning effort medium\",\n    \"usage\": \"unknown\"\n  },\n  \"testingFeedback\": [\n    \"About twenty defects, found by the bot runs and the sim checks (estimate).\",\n    \"Six were critical: combat damage that never reached the counters, a key that never reached the pack, a door the bot closed behind itself, a stand cell on the far side of a door, a hand emptied before a throw, and a stall while a monster stood near.\",\n    \"The most helpful test was the floor-one bot trace that printed each goal change with the hand contents.\",\n    \"The least helpful test was the browser smoke test, which checks for errors and the first screens, not play.\"\n  ],\n  \"engineFeedback\": [\n    \"Most liked: the 3D world API (a fixed camera, things, mobs as cards, the pen) and the 2D engine's game.debug and input.tap / hold for tests.\",\n    \"Got stuck: the 3D things list has no plate or stair, so we drew them; the input presets merge with our own action names in ways the API card does not spell out.\",\n    \"Most important thing we built ourselves: the sim, the bot, the wiring, the dungeon presenter and every screen.\",\n    \"Hardest part: the input and menu details (custom action names, pause menu items, settings), which the API card only sketches.\",\n    \"Changed in the engine: none.\",\n    \"One thing to change: ship the common things (plate, stair, a door