{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CghFbfpSnD3D1YRWLVwih","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The build runs and the tests pass, but the goal's condition is not met, so this is a partial delivery. Here's where it stands.\n\n## Status\n\n**Not complete.** The bundle, exit interview, docs and test command are in place, but the goal's \"done when\" is not satisfied:\n\n- **Floor 3 is not cleared.** The walkthrough bot clears floors 1 and 2 and then dies on floor 3 (at about 1141 s of game time). Floor 4, the Bolt-Holder fight, the ending, and the Veil-refused branch are not verified.\n- **AI Hub multiplayer is not built.** The session client is inlined and the page metas are set, but there is no ghost race, card, progress reporting, or harness run.\n- **Babble voices are not built.** Voices are not in the audio.\n- **Creation is Quick Start only.** There is no per-slot editor, name entry, or re-rolls.\n- **Glyphs are text.** Prompts show key names. There is no PlayStation or Xbox glyph painter and no button-symbol setting.\n- **Attract mode is untested past the title.** It runs the bot through five vignettes with cheats, and any key returns to the title.\n- **Time in menus is not applied.** The setting is defined but doesn't change the time scale.\n- **Art is simplified.** Most monsters are blob or humanoid cards, the item models are coloured boxes, and the view is still dim.\n\nWhat works, verified: the bundle opens from `file://` with no errors, New Game → Quick Start → intro → play runs, the sim is deterministic with a save round-trip, the maps and wiring pass lint, and the bot clears floors 1 and 2 with a real take, stow, pathing and combat loop.\n\n## Deliverables\n\n- Bundle: `work/EyeOfTheBoltHolder-EyeOfTheBeholder1991-claude-haiku-5-5-medium-20261103-202616.html` (1.7 MB, one file).\n- Exit interview: `work/exit-interview.json` (parses; all fields answered).\n- Dev folder: `work/EyeOfTheBoltHolder-EyeOfTheBeholder1991-claude-haiku-5-5-medium-20261103-202616/` with README, PATCHES (none), CONTENT, and the sources.\n- Test command: `node tests/run.mjs` → **175 passed, 0 failed · 4 suites · 17.2 s**.\n\n**Choices I made:**\n- Used the title from PLAN.md. I didn't re-run its RNG claim.\n- Built the sim, bot and screens myself. I didn't use the engine's E.Grid, because a small breadth-first search was simpler.\n- Did not patch the engine.\n\n## Source Information\n\n- Date: 2026-11-03 20:26:16\n- Source: Eye of the Beholder (1991, Westwood Associates / SSI)\n- Plan: PLAN.md\n- Genre and Perspective: real-time, first-person, grid-based party RPG dungeon crawler; first-person party view with tweened steps and quarter turns, plus a top-down automap\n- Tech: my-3D2dge 2D and 3D v0.85.2; three.js r182; Rapier 0.19.3 (jsDelivr); AI Hub session client 1.4.0; Node 24; Playwright 1.63.0\n- Art Direction: the engine's native low-resolution 3D look, code-drawn walls and things, cards for monsters, brass UI\n- Animation: engine rigs and blob bodies, tweened first-person camera with bob and bump, drawn wind-ups, doors and gates that rise, a pen-drawn boss eye (partial)\n- Audio: engine chip synth, step-sequencer songs and synthesized effects; no audio files; no babble voices\n- Online: session client and metas only; ghost race not built\n- Testing: `node tests/run.mjs` (lint, sim, bot, browser smoke), 175 checks\n- Research: engine API card, 3D manual and the starter crawler kit; no web research\n- Environment: Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux (WSL2); headless Chromium 1243 via Playwright\n- Model: Anthropic, claude-haiku-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- Usage: unknown\n\n## Testing Feedback\n\n- **Issues caught:** about 20 (estimate), found by the bot traces and the sim checks.\n- **Critical:** six stopped runs: combat damage that never reached the counters; a key that never reached the pack; a door the bot closed behind itself; a stand cell on the far side of a door; a hand emptied before a throw; a stall while a monster stood near.\n- **Most helpful test:** the floor-one bot trace that printed each goal change with the hand contents.\n- **Least helpful test:** the browser smoke test. It checks for errors and the first screens, not play.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n\n- **Liked most:** the 3D world API (fixed camera, things, mobs as cards, the pen), and the 2D engine's `game.debug` and `input.tap` / `hold` for tests.\n- **Stuck or guessed wrong:** the 3D things list has no plate or stair, so I drew them. The input presets merge with custom action names in ways the API card doesn't spell out.\n- **Most important thing built ourselves:** the sim, the bot, the wiring, the presenter and every screen.\n- **Hardest part:** the input and menu details (custom action names, pause items, settings).\n- **Changed in the engine:** none.\n- **One thing to change:** ship common things (plate, stair, a door variant) in the 3D library, and document the input map in one table.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n\n- **Liked most:** the exact maps, ids and tables. They made the content checkable.\n- **Confusing:** some numbers don't follow the plan's own formulas (Durgan's HP); \"silent\" teleporters are described two ways; the plan asks for E.Grid where a simpler search works.\n- **Hardest:** holding every system to full depth in one session. The spec is larger than one session.\n- **Would change:** a cut list per milestone that says what to drop first, plus an acceptance list per floor."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":972,"cache_read_input_tokens":613065,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":972},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c642ce04-34f8-46f2-be98-ceed51