{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CghG17L11QHZjGkZG128m","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The goal's condition is still not met. This turn I closed several of the listed gaps, but floors 3 and 4 and the AI Hub multiplayer are still open. I'm not calling the feature list complete.\n\n## Closed this turn\n\n- **Creation editor:** four roster slots, each built through race, class, stats, look and name. Stats are 4d6 drop-lowest, re-rolled until the class minimums are met. Quick Start fills the premade four. Starting gear and prepared spells follow the plan.\n- **Glyphs:** prompts show PlayStation glyphs by default. A \"Button symbols\" setting switches to Xbox (A, B, X, Y) when a pad is in use; otherwise key names show.\n- **Time in menus:** the setting now sets the game's time scale while a screen or Dev Mode is open (pause, slow or real time).\n- **Babble voices:** a WebAudio formant synth speaks each vowel of dialogue, with a base pitch per speaker. I haven't listened to it.\n- **Dead menu entries:** the memorize, formation, save and load screens now have real rows.\n- **Dev Mode:** the Spawn and Party tabs have real rows.\n\n## Still not met\n\n- **Floor 3 and 4:** the walkthrough bot clears floors 1 and 2 and dies on floor 3 at about 1141 s. An attempt to make the bot engage nearby monsters made floor 2 worse, so I reverted it. Floor 4, the Bolt-Holder fight and the ending are unverified, and the Veil-refused branch is untested.\n- **AI Hub multiplayer:** not built beyond the inlined session client and page metas. There is no ghost race, card, progress reporting, or harness run.\n- **Dev Mode Debug tab:** auto-play only. Sound test, overlays and waypoints are missing.\n- **Attract mode and touch notice:** implemented but not checked in a browser beyond the title.\n- **Art:** most monsters are cards or blobs, item models are coloured boxes, and the view is still dim.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `node tests/run.mjs`: 175 passed, 0 failed, 4 suites, 16.4 s. This covers lint, sim determinism and save round-trip, the bot reaching floor 2, and the browser opening the bundle from `file://`.\n- `tests/browser-play.mjs`: Quick Start, intro and play load with no errors.\n- Bundle: `work/EyeOfTheBoltHolder-EyeOfTheBeholder1991-claude-haiku-5-5-medium-20261103-202616.html`. Exit interview: `work/exit-interview.json` (parses).\n\n## Source Information\n\n- Date: 2026-11-03 20:26:16\n- Source: Eye of the Beholder (1991, Westwood Associates / SSI)\n- Plan: PLAN.md\n- Genre and Perspective: real-time, first-person, grid-based party RPG dungeon crawler; first-person party view with tweened steps, plus a top-down automap\n- Tech: my-3D2dge 2D and 3D v0.85.2; three.js r182; Rapier 0.19.3; AI Hub client 1.4.0; Node 24; Playwright 1.63.0\n- Art Direction: the engine's low-resolution 3D look, code-drawn things, cards for monsters, brass UI\n- Animation: engine rigs, tweened camera, drawn wind-ups, pen-drawn boss eye (partial)\n- Audio: engine chip synth songs and effects; babble formant synth (unverified by ear)\n- Online: session client and metas only; ghost race not built\n- Testing: `node tests/run.mjs` (175 checks) and the browser play check\n- Research: engine API card, 3D manual, starter crawler kit; no web research\n- Environment: Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux (WSL2); headless Chromium 1243\n- Model: Anthropic, claude-haiku-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- Usage: unknown\n\n## Testing Feedback\n\n- **Issues caught:** about 20 (estimate), from bot traces and sim checks.\n- **Critical:** six stopped runs. Combat damage never reached the counters. A key never reached the pack. A door was toggled closed behind the bot. A stand cell was on the far side of a door. A hand was emptied before a throw. A stall while a monster stood near.\n- **Most helpful:** the floor-one trace that printed goal changes with hand contents.\n- **Least helpful:** the browser smoke test, which checks for errors and the first screens, not play.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n\n- **Liked most:** the World3D API (fixed camera, things, mobs as cards, the pen), and `game.debug` with `input.tap` / `hold` for tests.\n- **Stuck:** the 3D things list has no plate or stair, so I drew them. The input presets merge with custom action names in ways the API card doesn't spell out.\n- **Built ourselves:** the sim, bot, wiring, presenter, every screen, and now the creation editor and babble synth.\n- **Hardest:** input and menu details (custom action names, pause items, settings).\n- **Changed in the engine:** none.\n- **One change:** ship common things (plate, stair, a door variant) in the 3D library, and document the input map in one table.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n\n- **Liked most:** exact maps, ids and tables, which made the content checkable.\n- **Confusing:** some numbers don't follow the plan's formulas (Durgan's HP); \"silent\" teleporters are described two ways; the plan asks for E.Grid where a simple search does the job.\n- **Hardest:** holding every system to full depth in one session.\n- **Would change:** a cut list per milestone, and an acceptance list per floor."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1417,"cache_read_input_tokens":639126,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1417},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c642ce04-34f8-46f2-be98-ceed51703e52","uuid":"f5b00b66-1d9a-4432-9201-d8b2b63bffcb","timestamp":"2026-11-04T04:30:35.984Z","request_id":"req_011CghG16zuEDnkDpv8aojY4"}
