{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CghHfgVhzsHxc66obB3CX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The goal's condition is still not met. The bundle and exit interview are in place, but several TASK.md features are either incomplete or only verified under god mode.\n\n## What changed this turn\n\n- **AI Hub ghost race:** built and verified against the hub's own harness. Passes for 2 players, 4 players with latency and loss, and the host-leave case (rerun twice; one earlier run failed on a timing check and the Enter handling was then made more tolerant).\n- **Dev Mode Debug tab:** now has the cell and facing overlay, monster state overlay, wiring overlay (text lines, rough), waypoints for the current floor, a sound test covering every sound, and a song list.\n- **Creation editor:** four slots, each built through race, class, stats (4d6 drop-lowest, re-rolled to class minimums), look and name. Quick Start fills the premade four.\n- **Glyphs and time in menus:** PlayStation or Xbox words by setting; time scale follows the \"Time in menus\" setting.\n- **Babble voices:** a formant synth speaks dialogue vowels. Not checked by ear.\n- **Floor 3 walk and bot fixes:** the warded lock L3 was never tried, the Undergate needs three separate inserts, and held items were being put into the reliquary alcove. Fixed.\n- **Bolt-Holder and floor probes:** under god mode the boss reaches phase 3, dies, and the Great Lock stair ends the game with a victory. Floor 3 and floor 2 run through their goals under god mode.\n\n## Still not met\n\n- **Floor 3 at normal balance:** the bot dies in the Gauntlet fight. Wardens do most of the damage, with reach-2 attacks the party's melee can't answer, and party levels lag because downed members miss kill XP. I tried lowering monster damage; it didn't clear the floor, so I reverted it to the plan's 1.0. This is a balance problem, not a sim crash.\n- **Floor 4 and the Bolt-Holder at normal balance:** not played. The lock-turning path wasn't exercised by the probe, because the bot attacked the boss directly.\n- **Veil-refused branch:** not tested.\n- **Solo Rat Run best-run ghost:** not built.\n- **Glyphs:** prompts use glyph words, not drawn shapes.\n- **Monsters and item art:** simple cards and blobs. The Debug overlays are text lines.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `node tests/run.mjs --fast`: 173 passed, 0 failed, 6 suites.\n- `tests/run.mjs boss browser`: 2 passed, 0 failed.\n- `tests/run.mjs hub`: passes for all three harness runs (one earlier flaky failure, then two clean reruns of the host-leave case).\n- Bundle: `work/EyeOfTheBoltHolder-EyeOfTheBeholder1991-claude-haiku-5-5-medium-20261103-202616.html`. Exit interview: `work/exit-interview.json` (parses).\n\n## Source Information\n\n- Date: 2026-11-03 20:26:16\n- Source: Eye of the Beholder (1991, Westwood Associates / SSI)\n- Plan: PLAN.md\n- Genre and Perspective: real-time, first-person, grid-based party RPG dungeon crawler; first-person party view with tweened steps, plus a top-down automap\n- Tech: my-3D2dge 2D and 3D v0.85.2; three.js r182 (WebGL 2 forced); Rapier 0.19.3; AI Hub client 1.4.0; Node 24; Playwright 1.63.0\n- Art Direction: the engine's low-resolution 3D look, code-drawn things, cards for monsters, brass UI\n- Animation: engine rigs and blob bodies, tweened camera, drawn wind-ups, pen-drawn boss eye (partial)\n- Audio: engine chip synth songs and effects; babble formant synth (not checked by ear)\n- Online: AI Hub ghost race, 1 to 4 players, verified by the hub's harness; solo best-run ghost not built\n- Testing: `tests/run.mjs` suites (lint, sim, bot, boss, hub, browser) plus floor probes\n- Research: engine API card, 3D manual, starter crawler kit, AI Hub README; no web research\n- Environment: Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux (WSL2); headless Chromium 1243\n- Model: Anthropic, claude-haiku-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- Usage: unknown\n\n## Testing Feedback\n\n- **Issues caught:** about 30 (estimate), from bot traces, sim checks and the hub harness.\n- **Critical:** the most serious stopped runs: damage that never reached the counters; a key that never reached the pack; a door toggled closed behind the bot; a stand cell past a closed door; a hand emptied before a throw; a stall while a monster stood near; a wand never used because the bot picked a scroll a fighter can't read; held items placed into an alcove by mistake.\n- **Most helpful:** the goal-by-goal trace that printed hand contents, and the floor probes under god mode, which separated mechanics bugs from balance problems.\n- **Least helpful:** the browser smoke test, which checks only for errors and the first screens.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n\n- **Liked most:** the World3D API (fixed camera, things, mobs as cards), and the 2D engine's `game.debug` and input helpers for tests.\n- **Stuck:** the 3D things list has no plate or stair, so I drew them. The 3D init defaults to WebGPU, which produced \"instance dropped\" errors under four concurrent pages until I forced WebGL.\n- **Built ourselves:** the sim, the bot, the wiring, the presenter, every screen, the creation editor and the hub module.\n- **Hardest:** the input and menu details, and the hub's timing when games load in parallel.\n- **Changed in the engine:** none.\n- **One change:** ship common things (plate, stair, a door variant) in the 3D library, and state in the API card that the default backend is WebGPU and that WebGL needs an explicit option.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n\n- **Liked most:** exact maps, ids and tables, which made the content checkable; and the explicit list of hub checks.\n- **Confusing:** some numbers don't follow the plan's formulas (Durgan's HP); \"silent\" teleporters are described two ways; the plan's wording on \"time in menus\" and on the Veil branches doesn't say what is observable.\n- **Hardest:** holding every system to full depth, and balancing combat without a playtest loop.\n- **Would change:** a cut list per milestone, and a per-floor acceptance list that separates mechanics from balance."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1692,"cache_read_input_tokens":723719,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1692},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c642ce04-34f8-46f2-be98-ceed51703e52","uuid":"d1b91f4f-e882-4233-9993-34957e9664c4","timestamp":"2026-11-04T04:52:24.770Z","request_id":"req_011CghHfg8dskq2JHHqqnpjE"}
