{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CghJ3UwYqEDfgMNa49pK7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The goal's condition is still not met, and I'm not going to claim it is. The bundle and exit interview exist and parse, but a few TASK.md requirements are unfinished or only checked under god mode.\n\n## Closed this turn\n\n- **Solo Rat Run best-run ghost:** the party's trail is recorded at 10 Hz, the best time and trail are kept in local storage, and a golden ghost is drawn from the best trail in solo runs.\n- **Veil-refused branch:** a separate walk (the barracks, LV4 and G9 route to the reliquary) gets the bot through floor 3 and onto floor 4 under god mode, with the iron ward obtained and H2 left shut.\n- **Drawn glyphs:** on a pad, HUD prompts are drawn shapes (PlayStation ○ ✕ □ △, or Xbox letters by setting). Keyboard prompts stay text.\n- **Bug fixed:** a broken apostrophe in the About text had stopped the bundle from loading. The bundle loads again.\n\n## Still open\n\n- **Floor 3 at normal balance:** not cleared. The party dies in the Gauntlet fight, mainly to the wardens' reach-2 attacks the party's melee can't answer. Party levels also lag, since members who are Down miss kill XP. A monster-damage cut didn't clear it, so I reverted to the plan's 1.0. This needs a real balance pass.\n- **Floor 4 and the Bolt-Holder at normal balance:** not played. Under god mode the boss reaches phase 3, dies, and the Great Lock stair ends the game with a victory. The lock-turning path isn't exercised by the probe.\n- **Veil-refused branch and floors 3–4:** checked for mechanics under god mode only.\n- **Babble voices:** not checked by ear.\n- **Art:** monsters are cards or simple blobs. The Debug overlays are text lines.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `tests/run.mjs --fast`: 173 passed, 0 failed.\n- `tests/run.mjs boss hub`: 4 passed, 0 failed (the boss probe and three hub harness runs).\n- Browser play check: 0 errors.\n- Bundle: `work/EyeOfTheBoltHolder-EyeOfTheBeholder1991-claude-haiku-5-5-medium-20261103-202616.html`. Exit interview: `work/exit-interview.json` (parses).\n\n## Source Information\n\n- Date: 2026-11-03 20:26:16\n- Source: Eye of the Beholder (1991, Westwood Associates / SSI)\n- Plan: PLAN.md\n- Genre and Perspective: real-time, first-person, grid-based party RPG dungeon crawler; first-person party view with tweened steps, plus a top-down automap\n- Tech: my-3D2dge 2D and 3D v0.85.2; three.js r182 (WebGL 2 forced); Rapier 0.19.3; AI Hub client 1.4.0; Node 24; Playwright 1.63.0\n- Art Direction: the engine's low-resolution 3D look, code-drawn things, cards for monsters, brass UI\n- Animation: engine rigs and blob bodies, tweened camera, drawn wind-ups, pen-drawn boss eye (partial)\n- Audio: engine chip synth songs and effects; babble formant synth (not checked by ear)\n- Online: AI Hub ghost race, 1 to 4 players, verified by the hub's harness; solo best-run ghost from a local trail\n- Testing: `tests/run.mjs` suites (lint, sim, bot, boss, hub, browser) and the floor probes\n- Research: engine API card, 3D manual, starter crawler kit, AI Hub README; no web research\n- Environment: Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux (WSL2); headless Chromium 1243\n- Model: Anthropic, claude-haiku-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- Usage: unknown\n\n## Testing Feedback\n\n- **Issues caught:** about 30 (estimate), from bot traces, sim checks, probes and the hub harness.\n- **Critical:** damage that never reached the counters; a key that never reached the pack; a door toggled closed behind the bot; a stand cell past a closed door; a hand emptied before a throw; a stall beside a monster; a wand skipped because the bot picked a scroll a fighter can't read; held items placed into an alcove by mistake; the Undergate taking one ward per visit.\n- **Most helpful:** the goal-by-goal trace with hand contents, and the god-mode probes, which separated mechanics bugs from balance problems.\n- **Least helpful:** the browser smoke test, which checks only for errors and the first screens.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n\n- **Liked most:** the World3D API (fixed camera, things, mobs as cards), and the 2D engine's `game.debug` and input helpers.\n- **Stuck:** the 3D things list has no plate or stair, so I drew them. The 3D init defaults to WebGPU, which gave \"instance dropped\" errors under four concurrent pages until I forced WebGL.\n- **Built ourselves:** the sim, bot, wiring, presenter, every screen, the creation editor, the hub module and the ghost.\n- **Hardest:** input and menu details, and hub timing when games load in parallel.\n- **Changed in the engine:** none.\n- **One change:** ship common things (plate, stair, a door variant) in the 3D library, and say in the API card that the default backend is WebGPU and WebGL needs an explicit option.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n\n- **Liked most:** exact maps, ids and tables, which made the content checkable; and the explicit hub checklist.\n- **Confusing:** some numbers don't follow the plan's formulas (Durgan's HP); \"silent\" teleporters are described two ways; the plan doesn't say what is observable for the Veil branches or time in menus.\n- **Hardest:** holding every system to full depth, and balancing combat without a playtest loop.\n- **Would change:** a cut list per milestone, and per-floor acceptance that separates mechanics from balance."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1121,"cache_read_input_tokens":737754,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1121},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c642ce04-34f8-46f2-be98-ceed51703e52","uuid":"d909997f-98a1-4ffa-84d6-10e32b043651","timestamp":"2026-11-04T04:57:17.729Z","request_id":"req_011CghJ3UZy8sjCDRABJTPS1"}
