{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CghJ5iALNmQGAVB3E843C","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The goal's condition is still not met, and I'm stopping here rather than repeating the same gaps.\n\n**Closed this turn:** the Great Lock path is now tested directly. Turning GL1 starts the two-second turn, the party can't act during it, and the lock ends turned with two bolts drawn back. The check is in the boss suite (`tests/run.mjs boss`: 2 passed).\n\n**Still open, and not closed by anything I ran:**\n- Floor 3 at normal balance is not cleared. The party dies in the Gauntlet fight, mostly to the wardens' reach-2 attacks, and party levels lag.\n- Floor 4 and the Bolt-Holder have not been played at normal balance. Under god mode the boss fight, the locks and the ending all run.\n- The Veil-refused branch and floors 3–4 were checked only under god mode.\n- Babble voices have not been checked by ear.\n\nThe next real step is a balance pass on floor 3 (warden damage and reach, XP sharing to Down members, party levels). That needs playtesting cycles I can't do well in this session, so I won't claim the features are complete.\n\n**Verification:** `tests/run.mjs --fast` passes 173 checks. `tests/run.mjs boss` passes 2 suites (boss probe, lock probe). `tests/run.mjs hub` passed on the previous build, and the hub code has not changed since.\n\n**Deliverables:** the bundle is at `work/EyeOfTheBoltHolder-EyeOfTheBeholder1991-claude-haiku-5-5-medium-20261103-202616.html` and `work/exit-interview.json` parses.\n\n**Source Information:** the fields are as in my last full report, with the testing line now including the lock probe. Usage is unknown.\n\n**Testing Feedback:**\n- About 30 defects found (estimate). Six or so stopped runs outright.\n- Most helpful: the goal trace with hand contents, plus the god-mode probes that separated mechanics bugs from balance problems.\n- Least helpful: the browser smoke test, which checks errors and first screens only.\n\n**Engine Feedback:**\n- Liked most: the World3D API (fixed camera, things, mobs as cards) and the 2D engine's `game.debug` and input helpers.\n- Stuck: the 3D library lacks plate and stair things, and it defaults to WebGPU, which errored under four concurrent pages until WebGL was forced.\n- Built ourselves: the sim, bot, wiring, presenter, screens, creation editor, hub module and ghost.\n- Changed in the engine: none.\n- One change: ship common things in the 3D library and state the default backend in the API card.\n\n**Prompt Feedback:**\n- Liked most: exact maps, ids and tables, and the explicit hub checklist.\n- Confusing: a few numbers don't match the plan's formulas (Durgan's HP), \"silent\" teleporters are described two ways, and the observable outcomes for Veil and time-in-menus aren't stated.\n- Hardest: holding every system to full depth, and balancing combat without playtest cycles.\n- Would change: a cut list per milestone, and per-floor acceptance that separates mechanics from balance.\n\nDo you want me to take on the floor 3 balance pass next, or accept the current build as a partial delivery?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":642,"cache_read_input_tokens":743152,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":642},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c642ce04-34f8-46f2-be98-ceed51703e52","uuid":"ff822e5d-3315-4acb-b668-6cabf21e7f04","timestamp":"2026-11-04T04:58:02.721Z","request_id":"req_011CghJ5hokg5BxSb3Zvxvz4"}
