{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CghJ7htXipX9ktSBUjxeg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The condition is not met, and I'm not going to claim it is. The build is partial.\n\n**Still open against TASK.md:**\n- Floor 3 at normal balance is not cleared. The party dies in the Gauntlet fight, mostly to the wardens' reach-2 attacks, and party levels lag.\n- Floor 4 and the Bolt-Holder have not been played at normal balance. Under god mode the boss fight, the Great Locks and the ending all run, and the lock turn is now tested directly.\n- The Veil-refused branch and floors 3–4 were checked only under god mode.\n- Babble voices have not been checked by ear.\n\nClearing floor 3 needs a balance pass on warden damage and reach, XP sharing to Down members, and party levels, followed by playtest cycles. I can't verify that well in this session, so I'm stopping rather than repeating the same checks.\n\n**Deliverables:**\n- Bundle: `work/EyeOfTheBoltHolder-EyeOfTheBeholder1991-claude-haiku-5-5-medium-20261103-202616.html`\n- Exit interview: `work/exit-interview.json` (parses, every field answered)\n- Tests: `node tests/run.mjs --fast` passes 173 checks; the boss suite passes 2 (boss probe and lock probe).\n\n**Source Information**\n- Date: 2026-11-03 20:26:16\n- Source: Eye of the Beholder (1991, Westwood Associates / SSI)\n- Plan: PLAN.md\n- Genre and Perspective: real-time, first-person, grid-based party RPG dungeon crawler; first-person party view with tweened steps, plus a top-down automap\n- Tech: my-3D2dge 2D and 3D v0.85.2; three.js r182 (WebGL 2 forced); Rapier 0.19.3; AI Hub client 1.4.0; Node 24; Playwright 1.63.0\n- Art Direction: the engine's low-resolution 3D look, code-drawn things, cards for monsters, brass UI\n- Animation: engine rigs and blob bodies, tweened camera, drawn wind-ups, pen-drawn boss eye (partial)\n- Audio: engine chip synth songs and effects; babble formant synth (not checked by ear)\n- Online: AI Hub ghost race, 1–4 players, passes the hub harness; solo best-run ghost from a local trail\n- Testing: `tests/run.mjs` suites (lint, sim, bot, boss, hub, browser) and the floor probes\n- Research: engine API card, 3D manual, starter crawler kit, AI Hub README; no web research\n- Environment: Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux (WSL2); headless Chromium 1243\n- Model: Anthropic, claude-haiku-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- Usage: unknown\n\n**Testing Feedback**\n- Issues caught: about 30 (estimate), from bot traces, sim checks, probes and the hub harness.\n- Critical: several stopped runs outright, including damage that never reached the counters, a key that never reached the pack, a door toggled shut behind the bot, and the Undergate taking only one ward per visit.\n- Most helpful: the goal-by-goal trace with hand contents, plus the god-mode probes that separated mechanics bugs from balance problems.\n- Least helpful: the browser smoke test, which checks only for errors and first screens.\n\n**Engine Feedback**\n- Liked most: the World3D API (fixed camera, things, mobs as cards) and the 2D engine's `game.debug` and input helpers.\n- Stuck: the 3D library lacks plate and stair things, and it defaults to WebGPU, which errored under four concurrent pages until WebGL was forced.\n- Built ourselves: the sim, bot, wiring, presenter, screens, creation editor, hub module and ghost.\n- Changed in the engine: none.\n- One change: ship common things in the 3D library, and state the default backend in the API card.\n\n**Prompt Feedback**\n- Liked most: exact maps, ids and tables, and the explicit hub checklist.\n- Confusing: some numbers don't match the plan's formulas (Durgan's HP), \"silent\" teleporters are described two ways, and the observable outcomes for the Veil branches and time-in-menus aren't stated.\n- Hardest: holding every system to full depth, and balancing combat without playtest cycles.\n- Would change: a cut list per milestone, and per-floor acceptance that separates mechanics from balance.\n\nI need your direction. Should I do the floor 3 balance pass now, which means several playtest cycles and likely more time, or do you accept this build as a partial delivery?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1570,"cache_read_input_tokens":743794,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1570},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c642ce04-34f8-46f2-be98-ceed51703e52","uuid":"f0d72c70-3fce-42d8-8e0a-570b4092546a","timestamp":"2026-11-04T04:58:14.482Z","request_id":"req_011CghJ7hUj7jbovMhyPkzfi"}
